// The render package: drawing lit 3D meshes on the GPU, through the gpu
// package (Vulkan underneath, and nothing of Vulkan's here). A program reaches
// it with 'import render', and gets:
//
// - Renderer, which owns what drawing needs: the pipelines of its materials,
//   the frame's uniforms, and the resources it hands out handles to --
//   meshes, textures, materials -- each kept in a generational pool (the
//   pool package), so a handle to something removed reaches nothing.
// - GpuMesh, a mesh.Mesh's vertex streams (positions, normals, uvs, each its
//   own vertex buffer, as the Mesh keeps them) and its 32-bit indices,
//   uploaded once into GPU buffers and kept; each of the mesh's material
//   groups is one draw. A MeshHandle names one, and its contents can be
//   replaced under the same handle ('replaceMesh'): the new version is
//   uploaded at once and drawn from the next frame on, and the old one's
//   buffers are released to the frame that last drew it, destroyed when the
//   GPU has finished it. That is what meshes that arrive at several levels
//   of detail, sculpted at run time, need. A dynamic mesh
//   ('addDynamicMesh') is room for a mesh rewritten in place frame by frame
//   ('writeDynamicMesh').
// - Giving back, for a world that is replaced by another: every handle is
//   released one by one, as 'removeMesh' does a mesh -- 'removeMaterial',
//   'removeTexture' (the textures a material was made with are the caller's
//   to remove: render keeps no list, and a texture may serve several
//   materials), 'RenderView.release' -- and the handle reaches nothing at
//   once. Nothing waits: the GPU memory is destroyed when the GPU has
//   finished the frames that may have used it (gpu's deletion queue,
//   'queue.releaseTexture'). Scene items and draws that still name a
//   removed material are skipped. 'resourceUse' counts what the renderer
//   holds (meshes, textures, materials, pipelines and their bytes).
//   Pipelines are not per world and have no release.
// - Custom pipelines (custom.cone): shaders of the caller's own
//   ('addPipeline'), importing renderframe.slang, whose materials
//   ('addCustomMaterial') bind parameters and textures of their own (an
//   r32float field from 'addFieldTexture', read in the vertex stage, for a
//   heightfield), drawn, batched and instanced with the rest.
// - LodChain, the levels of detail of one object, most detailed first
//   (LOD 0, as Unreal, Unity and Godot number them), chosen by index or by
//   the size the object is drawn at, with hysteresis so it does not flicker
//   at a threshold.
// - Camera (perspective or orthogonal, depth from 0 to 1, placed by origin
//   and orientation or 'lookAt') and Light (one directional light and
//   ambient light).
// - Material, the standard lit one: a base color times a texture (the
//   texture optional), Lambert diffuse and Blinn-Phong specular, and an
//   emissive color, in Slang (lit.slang); and lines in one flat color
//   (lines.slang), for wireframes and edges. Every material has an alpha
//   mode, glTF's: opaque, cut out (ALPHA_MASK: a fragment below the
//   cut-off is discarded; leaves, fences) or see-through (ALPHA_BLEND:
//   glass, glowing panes, light painted on with an alpha of 0).
// - One lighting convention for every material (renderframe.slang): the
//   light's color is irradiance (lux in physical units), ambient light,
//   sky and emissive colors are radiance (nits), and everything drawn is
//   multiplied by 'exposure' as it is written ('exposureFromEv100').
// - PbrMaterial, the physically based one (pbr.slang, over the brdf
//   module): glTF 2.0's metallic-roughness base (GGX, Smith, Schlick,
//   Lambert), a clear coat over it, and over the coat a thin film (Belcour
//   and Barla's iridescence) whose thickness is the noise package's warped
//   fBm, drifting with 'renderer.time'; lit by the sun and by the
//   Environment. Its base may come from glTF's maps: base colour,
//   metallic-roughness, occlusion and a tangent-space normal map, whose
//   tangents the shader finds from screen-space derivatives.
// - Sky (sky.slang), an analytic dusk, drawn behind the scene once set
//   ('setSky'); and Environment, the image-based lighting the renderer
//   makes from it by full-screen passes (ibl.slang): the sky's cube and its
//   levels, a specular cube prefiltered by roughness, a diffuse cube, and
//   the split sum's table (lighting.cone).
// - Post, from HDR light to the display (post.slang, post.cone): the
//   half-float frame the renderer draws into, Jimenez's bloom chain, and
//   tone mapping by AgX (or ACES's fit, Reinhard, none), and a finish after it
//   (colour grading by a 3-D table and lift / gamma / gain, a vignette, film grain).
// - Image quality (fx.cone and the files it names): 'ImageFx.render' draws the
//   scene and the optional passes around it: temporal anti-aliasing (jitter,
//   a velocity pass for what moves, a clipped reprojection, sharpening), FXAA,
//   auto-exposure (a luminance histogram in compute), SSAO (GTAO), depth of
//   field, volumetric fog (froxels, lit through the shadow cascades), and
//   decals; all off by default, with quality tiers for a discrete and an
//   integrated GPU. 'camera.jitterX' and 'jitterY' shift the projection.
// - Sun shadows (shadow.cone, shadowing.slang): 'setShadows' with a
//   ShadowSettings ('high', 'medium', 'low', 'off': 1 to 4 cascades, the
//   map's size, the filter) switches on cascaded shadow maps for the
//   directional light. Each cascade is the sun's orthographic view of a
//   slice of the camera's frustum (the practical split scheme, fitted to a
//   bounding sphere, snapped to texels so edges do not shimmer), drawn
//   depth only into one layer of a depth texture array before the scene;
//   the lit and physically based materials read it with percentage-closer
//   filtering over a rotated Poisson disk, receiver-plane depth bias and a
//   normal offset, blending cascades at their seams. Cut-out, skinned and
//   flutter meshes cast what they show; see-through and custom-pipeline
//   draws cast nothing, nor does an item marked 'dontCastShadow'.
// - The scene (visibility.cone, hiz.cone, fade.slang, hiz.slang): things that
//   stay, added with 'addSceneItem' (a SceneHandle each, a proxy in a
//   spatialindex.Bvh, refitted by 'moveSceneItem') and culled for every camera
//   that draws -- the main view, each shadow cascade, each local light's shadow
//   face, each RenderView, each reflection probe face -- with batches gathered
//   from what that camera sees alone. Levels of detail by projected size (the
//   item's LodChain, hysteresis, a bias a camera and a shadow pass can set) that
//   change by a dithered cross-fade; visibility ranges whose edges fade; and
//   occlusion by a hierarchical depth pyramid in two passes, the survivors
//   compacted on the GPU and drawn by indirect draws. 'renderer.vis.settings'
//   switches each off, and with all off the scene draws what a DrawList of its
//   items would. A DrawList still draws whole beside it.
// - The extended material (scenecapture.cone, pbrx.slang, lobes.slang, capture.slang): a
//   PbrMaterial that sets sheen, anisotropy, subsurface scattering, glass, screen-space
//   reflections, wet darkening or caustic reception is drawn by extended pipelines whose
//   fourth bind group is a capture of the frame drawn so far (colour pyramid, depth copy,
//   tables). Made when the first such material is added; the opaque pass is cut for each
//   capture. 'setReflections' tiers the ray march, 'setCaustics' places a caustic volume.
// - Point and spot lights (lights.cone, locallights.slang): real light
//   sources, in 'renderer.lights', named by handles and cheap to add, move,
//   aim, recolour and re-intensify every frame (a flicker). Intensity in
//   candela (so a scene in physical units lights with them and exposes with
//   'exposureFromEv100'), a falloff of the inverse square windowed to zero at
//   the light's range (Karis, UE4 2013), a spot's cone a smooth ramp between
//   inner and outer angles, a source's radius (a bulb) giving the highlight
//   its size (Karis's representative point). CLUSTERED FORWARD SHADING
//   (Olsson, Billeter and Assarsson 2012; Doom 2016; Godot 4): the view is a
//   grid of 16 x 9 x 24 froxels (depth exponential), the CPU assigns each
//   light to the froxels it reaches (at most 1,024 lights, 64 to a
//   cluster), and the lit and physically based materials loop over the
//   lights of their own fragment's cluster, over nothing in a scene without
//   any. A light and a material each have a mask of layers (bits 0 to 23),
//   and a light reaches only the materials it shares one with: a bulb on
//   layer 1 lights a lantern's own frame and not the path. A scene with no
//   light that reaches the view is drawn bit for bit as it was before.
//   Shadows (lightshadow.cone, 'setLightShadows'): a light marked to cast
//   gets one perspective view (a spot light's) or six (a point light's, a
//   cube's faces) of a depth texture array, the best ranked while layers
//   last, drawn by the sun's casters, filtered as the sun's is, biased in
//   texels at the receiver.
// - DrawList: what is drawn this frame, each a mesh, a material and a model
//   matrix (and a tint), drawn in one render pass.
// - Skinning (skin.cone, skinning.slang): a mesh bound to a skeleton's bones
//   by a Skin (four joints and weights a vertex), uploaded by
//   'addSkinnedMesh' and drawn by 'DrawList.addSkinned' with one skinning
//   matrix a bone, which the GPU blends (linear blend skinning) in the
//   skinned variants of the lit and physically based pipelines.
// - Morph targets (morph.cone, morph.slang): blend shapes, a mesh that changes
//   by a weighted sum of stored displacements. 'MorphTargets' holds them on the
//   CPU, a 'Morpher' uploads a set, makes morphed copies of a mesh (each a
//   MeshHandle of its own, drawn by any material, skinned or not, shadows
//   included) and runs a compute pre-pass on the frame's encoder before
//   'render' for the copies whose weights changed; morph first, then skin.
// - Views (views.cone): the scene drawn from another camera into a texture
//   of its own ('RenderView', rendered before the frame's main 'render', with a
//   layer mask over the draw list's items and a nesting limit), whose
//   picture any material samples ('ViewMaterials': a screen, a planar mirror,
//   reflective water with a Fresnel blend and a normal map's ripple); the
//   camera that sees in a mirror is 'camera.reflectedAbout(plane)' (camera.cone:
//   the world reflected, the mirror's plane the near plane by Lengyel's
//   oblique clip). And reflection probes ('addProbe': a cube captured at a
//   point, filtered like the sky by ibl.slang's pipelines), which light the
//   physically based copies inside the probe's box, box-projected.
// - Image, pixels from BMP (or made: 'Image.checker'), written as BMP too;
//   'addTexture' hands one to the GPU as sRGB colour, 'addLinearTexture' as
//   numbers (an ORM map), 'addNormalTexture' as a normal map; each with its
//   whole mip chain (mips.cone), which the renderer's sampler filters
//   trilinearly and anisotropically (16 where the device can).
//
// A frame, once a window, a device and a swapchain are open (the window and
// gpu packages):
//
//   mut renderer = Renderer.create(&mut device, swapchain.format, TEXTURE_FORMAT_DEPTH32_FLOAT);
//   imm ball = renderer.addMesh(&mut device, &sphere);          // once
//   imm redMaterial = Material.plain(new Color(1., 0., 0., 1.));
//   imm red = renderer.addMaterial(&mut device, &redMaterial);
//   ...
//   imm frame = swapchain.getCurrentTexture(&mut device);
//   list.clear();
//   list.add(ball, red, Mat4.fromTranslation(new Vec3(0., 1., 0.)));
//   mut encoder = device.createCommandEncoder();
//   renderer.render(&mut device, &mut encoder, &frame.texture, &frame.depth, &camera, &light, &list);
//   device.queue.submit(encoder.finish());
//   swapchain.present(&mut device);
//
// Lit physically, in HDR: the renderer draws into a Post's half-float frame,
// and the Post bloom and tone-map it into the swapchain's texture (post.cone
// has the frame's shape).
//
// HOW IT IS BOUND. Group 0 is the frame's (renderframe.slang): one uniform
// buffer holding the camera's view-projection matrix, its inverse and
// position, the light, the target's size, the time, the environment's
// strength and the exposure, and one storage buffer of instances, each
// drawn copy's model matrix and tint (80 bytes), both written once a render
// ('queue.writeBuffer'); then, read by the skinned vertex stages only
// (skinning.slang), the bones (a storage buffer of every skinned copy's
// skinning matrices, 48 bytes a bone, each copy's run side by side) and the
// bone bases (a storage buffer of a u32 an instance: where its copy's bones
// start, or NO_BONES), both written once a render too; then the sun's
// shadows (shadowparams.slang, shadowing.slang): their parameters in a
// uniform buffer (binding 4), the cascades' depth texture array (5) and the
// comparison sampler that reads it (6), a one-texel stand-in while shadows
// are off; then the point and spot lights (locallights.slang): the clusters'
// parameters in a uniform buffer (binding 7), the lights in a storage buffer
// (8, four float4s a light) and the clusters' lists in another (9: an offset
// and a count a cluster, then the lists). The shadow passes bind a group of
// their own (bindings 0 to 4, without the map they draw into). Group 1 is the material's: its parameters in a
// uniform buffer of its own, its texture and the renderer's sampler; for
// the physically based material, its metallic-roughness, normal and
// occlusion maps after them (its own layout, 'pbrMaterialLayout'); for a
// custom pipeline's material, its parameters, its textures and the sampler,
// as its pipeline lays them out (custom.cone). Group 2, bound for the
// physically based material, the sky and a custom pipeline that asks, is
// the environment's: the sky's parameters, its cubes and table, their
// sampler. Lines take their model matrix and color from the
// immediates (Vulkan's push constants) instead, one draw each.
//
// INSTANCING. The draw list's items are gathered into batches, one per
// (material, mesh): the copies of one mesh in one material, however many
// items name them, are one instanced draw per material group of the mesh
// ('drawIndexed' with an instance count and a first instance), their
// instances side by side in the instance buffer. A scene of a thousand
// stones in one material is one draw. Copies of one skinned mesh batch the
// same way, each with bones of its own, found through its bone base.
//
// THE DRAW ORDER. Opaque draws are sorted batch by batch, meshes
// (Blinn-Phong or physically based, by their material; cut-out ones among
// them) before lines, front to back by the distance from the camera to the
// nearest model origin of the batch, so nearer surfaces fill the depth
// buffer first and hide what is behind them before it is shaded. The sky
// comes next, where nothing was drawn (depth tested at the far plane). Then
// the see-through draws (a material whose alpha mode is ALPHA_BLEND, or a
// custom pipeline made so): sorted copy by copy, back to front by the
// distance to the centre of each copy's bounding sphere, blended with
// premultiplied alpha, depth tested against the opaque surfaces but not
// written. They are still instanced: a run of copies of one mesh in one
// material that lie next to each other in that order is one draw, its
// instances back to front (Vulkan draws an instanced draw's instances in
// order), so the order is right copy by copy, and copies that do not
// interleave with others (a row of lantern panes) stay one draw. Sorting
// is by object, not by triangle: one mesh's own see-through faces are drawn
// in its index order.
//
// Its files are one module, and only this one, the root, imports:
//
//   render.cone    Renderer and DrawList
//   gpumesh.cone   GpuMesh, mesh slots and handles, LodChain
//   material.cone  Material, material and texture slots and handles; lit.slang's and lines.slang's SPIR-V
//   custom.cone    CustomPipeline, pipeline slots and handles: the contract a custom pipeline keeps
//   skin.cone      Skin, the bones' layout, the CPU's twin of skinning.slang
//   lighting.cone  Sky, PbrMaterial, Environment; pbr.slang's and ibl.slang's SPIR-V
//   post.cone      Post: the HDR frame, bloom, tone mapping; post.slang's SPIR-V
//   camera.cone    Camera, Light
//   views.cone     RenderView, ViewMaterials, ReflectionProbe; viewmat.slang's and probe.slang's SPIR-V
//   image.cone     Image
//   morph.cone     MorphTargets, Morpher, MorphMixer; morph.slang's SPIR-V
//   shadow.cone    ShadowSettings, the cascades' maths, the shadow map and its casters' pipelines and passes;
//                  shadowcast.slang's, shadowcutlit.slang's and shadowcutpbr.slang's SPIR-V
//   fx.cone        ImageFx and FxSettings (the passes' order and tiers); taa.cone, fxaa.cone, exposure.cone,
//                  ssao.cone, dof.cone, fog.cone, decal.cone: each pass and its settings, with its shader's SPIR-V
//                  (taa.slang, taavelocity*.slang, fxaa.slang, autoexposure.slang, ssao.slang, dof.slang,
//                  fog.slang, decal.slang; the modules fxcommon and velocitycommon)
//   visibility.cone  Visibility (the scene, its hierarchy and levels), SceneHandle, VisibilitySettings, the fade code
//   hiz.cone       HiZ: the depth pyramid, its buffers and passes; hiz.slang's SPIR-V (fade.slang is the module
//                  lit.slang and pbr.slang import for the dither)
//   lights.cone    LightSet, LightHandle: point and spot lights, the froxel grid, the assignment and the
//                  GPU buffers (locallights.slang is the shaders' side of it)
//
// and its shaders, Slang: lit, lines, pbr, ibl and post, and the modules
// brdf, sky, renderframe, skinning, flutter, shadowparams, shadowing,
// locallights and shadowcasting they import (morph is a compute shader of its own) (pbr imports the noise package's too); the
// shadow casters shadowcast, shadowcutlit and shadowcutpbr draw depth only.
//
// Coordinates are geomath's and gpu's: right-handed, y up, the camera looking
// down its -z, clip space's y up and depth from 0 to 1. Faces wind
// counterclockwise seen from the front, as mesh's generators and sculpt's
// operators make them, and back faces are culled.

mod render;

import libc;
import gpu use *;
import geomath use *;
import collections use *;
import pool use *;
import mesh use Mesh, PolyMesh, Group;
import path use Path;
import spatialindex use Bvh, Proxy;

// Report a problem to stderr
fn logLine(msg &str) {
  var m = String.from(msg);
  m.appendByte('\n');
  let v &Array[u8] = m.view();
  libc.fflush(libc.stdout());
  libc.fwrite(v as *u8, 1usize, v.len, libc.stderr());
}

// The whole of a file, or ok false when it cannot be opened
fn readFile(path &Path, ok &mut bool) String {
  var text = String.empty();
  var cpath = String.from(path.view());
  let f = libc.fopen(cpath.cstr(), "rb");
  if !f {
    *ok = false;
    return text;
  }
  var buf = new Array[u8, 4096] <- fill 0u8;
  var going = true;
  while going {
    let n = libc.fread(&mut buf[0], 1usize, 4096usize, f);
    if n > 0usize { text.appendBytes(&buf[..<n]); }
    going = n == 4096usize;
  }
  libc.fclose(f);
  *ok = true;
  text
}

// The bytes of the frame uniforms (renderframe.slang's Frame) and of the
// immediates
const FRAME_BYTES = 224u64;
const IMMEDIATE_BYTES = 80u32;
const MATERIAL_BYTES = 64u64;
// An instance's bytes (renderframe.slang's Instance: a model matrix and a
// tint) and how many the instance buffer holds at first
const INSTANCE_BYTES = 80u64;
const INSTANCE_FLOATS = 20usize;
const FIRST_INSTANCES = 1024u32;

// What a material slot holds: the Blinn-Phong material, or the physically
// based one
const MATERIAL_BLINN_PHONG = 0u32;
const MATERIAL_PBR = 1u32;
const MATERIAL_CUSTOM = 2u32;

// The pipelines a draw may be bound to
const BOUND_NONE = 0u32;
const BOUND_LIT = 1u32;
const BOUND_LINES = 2u32;
const BOUND_PBR = 3u32;
const BOUND_CUSTOM = 4u32;
const BOUND_LIT_SKINNED = 5u32;
const BOUND_PBR_SKINNED = 6u32;
const BOUND_LIT_BLEND = 7u32;
const BOUND_PBR_BLEND = 8u32;
const BOUND_LIT_SKINNED_BLEND = 9u32;
const BOUND_PBR_SKINNED_BLEND = 10u32;
const BOUND_PBR_SWAY = 11u32;
const BOUND_PBRX = 12u32;
const BOUND_PBRX_SKINNED = 13u32;
const BOUND_PBRX_BLEND = 14u32;
const BOUND_PBRX_SKINNED_BLEND = 15u32;
const BOUND_PBRX_TANGENT = 16u32;
const BOUND_PBRX_GLASS = 17u32;

// The draw list's layers, in the order they are drawn: opaque meshes, then
// lines, then (after the sky) what is see-through
const LAYER_OPAQUE = 0u32;
const LAYER_LINES = 1u32;
const LAYER_BLEND = 2u32;

// What a renderer holds ('Renderer.resourceUse'): the counts of each kind of
// resource it hands out handles to, and the bytes of mesh buffers and texture
// levels
pub struct ResourceUse {
  pub meshes usize;
  pub meshBytes u64;
  pub textures usize;
  pub textureBytes u64;
  pub materials usize;
  pub pipelines usize;
}

// The bytes of a texture's levels, all of them
fn textureBytes(t &Texture) u64 {
  let texel = if t.format == TEXTURE_FORMAT_RGBA16_FLOAT { 8u64 } else { 4u64 };
  var w = u64.from(t.width);
  var h = u64.from(t.height);
  var total = 0u64;
  var level = 0u32;
  while level < t.mipLevelCount {
    total = total + w * h * texel * u64.from(t.depthOrArrayLayers);
    w = if w > 1u64 { w / 2u64 } else { 1u64 };
    h = if h > 1u64 { h / 2u64 } else { 1u64 };
    level = level + 1u32;
  }
  total
}

// What each render pass draws with: the renderer's pipelines, bind groups and
// the resources it hands out handles to
pub struct Renderer {
  pub colorFormat u32;             // the targets it draws into (TEXTURE_FORMAT_...)
  pub depthFormat u32;
  pub litShader ShaderModule;
  pub linesShader ShaderModule;
  pub frameLayout BindGroupLayout;
  pub materialLayout BindGroupLayout;
  pub layout PipelineLayout;
  pub litPipeline RenderPipeline;
  pub linesPipeline RenderPipeline;
  pub frameUniforms Buffer;
  pub frameGroup BindGroup;
  pub sampler Sampler;
  pub meshes Pool[MeshSlot];
  pub textures Pool[TextureSlot];
  pub materials Pool[MaterialSlot];
  pub white TextureHandle;         // 1 x 1, white: a material's texture when it has none
  pub pending List[MeshHandle];    // meshes replaced, to be swapped in at a frame's start
  pub drawCalls u32;               // how many draws the last render made
  pub triangles u64;               // and how many triangles (or lines) they drew
  pub pbrShader ShaderModule;
  pub environmentLayout BindGroupLayout;
  pub pbrLayout PipelineLayout;    // the frame, a material, the environment; the immediates
  pub pbrPipeline RenderPipeline;
  pub skyPipeline RenderPipeline;  // the sky behind the scene
  pub environment Environment;     // the image-based lighting made from the sky
  pub drawSky bool;                // draw the sky behind the scene ('setSky')
  pub time f32;                    // seconds: what the physically based material's film drifts by
  pub environmentStrength f32;     // how strongly the environment lights (1: as the sky is)
  pub pbrMaterialLayout BindGroupLayout;   // a physically based material's group: materialLayout's, then its three maps
  pub instances Buffer;            // every copy a render draws: its model matrix and tint (renderframe.slang's Instance)
  pub instanceCapacity u32;        // how many the buffer holds; grown by doubling
  pub instanceData List[f32];      // the copies' bytes, gathered on the CPU before one write
  pub keys List[DrawKey];          // the draw list's items sorted into batches
  pub batches List[DrawBatch];     // and the batches, in the order they are drawn
  pub instancesDrawn u32;          // how many copies the last render drew
  pub pipelines Pool[PipelineSlot];   // custom pipelines (custom.cone)
  pub litSkinnedPipeline RenderPipeline;   // the lit material, for a skinned mesh (lit.slang's vertexSkinned)
  pub pbrSkinnedPipeline RenderPipeline;   // and the physically based one (pbr.slang's)
  pub bones Buffer;                // every skinned copy's skinning matrices (skinning.slang's BoneXform)
  pub boneCapacity u32;            // how many it holds; grown by doubling
  pub boneBases Buffer;            // each instance's first bone, or NO_BONES; as many as the instances
  pub boneBaseData List[u32];      // gathered on the CPU before one write
  pub bonesDrawn u32;              // how many bones the last render wrote
  // The see-through (ALPHA_BLEND) variants of the lit and physically based
  // pipelines and of their skinned ones: blended with premultiplied alpha,
  // the depth tested, not written
  pub litBlendPipeline RenderPipeline;
  pub pbrBlendPipeline RenderPipeline;
  pub litSkinnedBlendPipeline RenderPipeline;
  pub pbrSkinnedBlendPipeline RenderPipeline;
  pub blendedDrawn u32;            // how many see-through copies the last render drew
  // The physically based pipeline for a mesh with a SWAY stream (gpumesh.cone)
  // drawn with a flutter material: a fourth vertex buffer, the colors
  pub pbrSwayPipeline RenderPipeline;
  // The sun's shadows (shadow.cone): off until 'setShadows'
  pub shadow ShadowState;
  // The point and spot lights (lights.cone): none until some are added
  pub lights LightSet;
  // The reflection probes ('addProbe', views.cone): a physically based copy
  // inside a probe's box is lit by that probe's cubes instead of the sky's
  pub probes List[ProbeSlot];
  // The scene: things that stay, culled for each camera and drawn at a level
  // of detail chosen by their size (visibility.cone)
  pub vis Visibility;
  // The depth pyramid that culls it (hiz.cone): none until occlusion is first on
  pub hiz List[HiZ];
  // The items the last render drew from, when it had a scene: the draw list's, then the scene's survivors
  // (a batch's keys name items by their place here). The passes after render that go by the batches
  // (temporal AA's motion, in fx.cone and taa.cone) read items from it, not from the draw list, whose
  // length the scene's items go past. 'frameItemsLive' is false when the last render had no scene (the
  // batches' keys then name the draw list's own items).
  pub frameItems List[DrawItem];
  // The extended material's machinery (scenecapture.cone): one, once a material that needs it (sheen,
  // anisotropy, subsurface, glass, reflections) was added; none before
  pub ext List[SceneCapture];
  // How hard screen-space reflections try ('setReflections')
  pub reflections ReflectionSettings;
  // The ray-traced scene (raytrace.cone): one, once ray tracing was asked for on a device that has it ('setRayTracing');
  // with it, 'ext' holds a second set of extended pipelines (ext[1]) that cast rays into it. None on a card without.
  pub rt List[RtScene];
  // The caustic volume 'setCaustics' last gave, for the extended pipelines made after it
  pub causticVolume CausticVolume;
  // Whether the extended material is ray-traced where it can be: set by 'setRayTracing'; and which of 'ext'
  // the render in progress draws with (0 raster, 1 ray-traced)
  pub rayTracing bool = false;
  pub extActive usize = 0usize;
  pub frameItemsLive bool = false;
  // Store the depth buffer at the end of 'render' (it is discarded
  // otherwise), so that a later pass into the same target -- glowing
  // particles drawn additively, say -- is depth tested against the scene
  pub keepDepth bool = false;
  // What every material's output, the sky's and the background's are
  // multiplied by before they are written (pre-exposure: the frame then
  // holds numbers near 1 however bright the scene's units). 1 for a scene
  // lit in display units; 'exposureFromEv100' for one in physical units
  // (the light in lux, ambient, sky and emissive in nits).
  pub exposure f32 = 1.;
  // A set of more keys than this is grouped by hash, not sorted (gatherSet): the
  // same batches, their copies in list order instead of nearest first
  pub bucketMin usize = 2048usize;
  // Whether the render in progress can capture its target (set by 'render' for the targets it can sample)
  pub captureReady bool = false;
  // The frames rendered so far, which the reflection march's noise turns with
  pub frameNumber u32 = 0u32;

  // A renderer drawing into targets of 'colorFormat', with a depth texture
  // of 'depthFormat' (TEXTURE_FORMAT_DEPTH32_FLOAT). For physically based
  // lighting, 'colorFormat' is TEXTURE_FORMAT_RGBA16_FLOAT and the target a
  // Post's frame, which tone-maps it to the display. Check 'isValid'.
  pub fn create(device &mut Device, colorFormat u32, depthFormat u32) Renderer {
    var litShader = device.createShaderModule(&LIT_SPIRV);
    var linesShader = device.createShaderModule(&LINES_SPIRV);
    // The frame's group: its uniforms, the instances, the bones and the
    // instances' bone bases (read-only storage)
    // and the sun's shadows: their parameters, the cascades' map (a depth
    // texture array) and the comparison sampler that reads it
    let frameEntries = [new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 0u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_VERTEX | SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 1u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_VERTEX | SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT,
        bufferType: BUFFER_BINDING_TYPE_READ_ONLY_STORAGE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 2u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_VERTEX, bufferType: BUFFER_BINDING_TYPE_READ_ONLY_STORAGE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 3u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_VERTEX, bufferType: BUFFER_BINDING_TYPE_READ_ONLY_STORAGE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 4u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_VERTEX | SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 5u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE,
        viewDimension: TEXTURE_VIEW_DIMENSION_2D_ARRAY, sampleType: TEXTURE_SAMPLE_TYPE_DEPTH),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 6u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_SAMPLER),
      // and the point and spot lights (locallights.slang): the clusters'
      // parameters, the lights, and the clusters' lists
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 7u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 8u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, bufferType: BUFFER_BINDING_TYPE_READ_ONLY_STORAGE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 9u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, bufferType: BUFFER_BINDING_TYPE_READ_ONLY_STORAGE),
      // and those lights' shadow views, a depth texture array (read through binding 6's comparison sampler)
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 10u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE,
        viewDimension: TEXTURE_VIEW_DIMENSION_2D_ARRAY, sampleType: TEXTURE_SAMPLE_TYPE_DEPTH)];
    var frameLayout = device.createBindGroupLayout(&frameEntries);
    let materialEntries = [new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 0u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 1u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 2u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_SAMPLER)];
    var materialLayout = device.createBindGroupLayout(&materialEntries);
    let groupLayouts = [&frameLayout, &materialLayout];
    var layout = device.createPipelineLayout(&groupLayouts, IMMEDIATE_BYTES);

    // The physically based material and the sky: a third group, the
    // environment's (the sky's parameters, the diffuse and specular cubes,
    // the split sum's table, their sampler)
    var pbrShader = device.createShaderModule(&PBR_SPIRV);
    let environmentEntries = [new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 0u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 1u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE,
        viewDimension: TEXTURE_VIEW_DIMENSION_CUBE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 2u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE,
        viewDimension: TEXTURE_VIEW_DIMENSION_CUBE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 3u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 4u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_SAMPLER)];
    var environmentLayout = device.createBindGroupLayout(&environmentEntries);
    // A physically based material's own group: the parameters, the base
    // colour's texture and the sampler, as the lit material's, then the
    // metallic-roughness, normal and occlusion maps
    // (the parameters are read by the vertex stage too: flutter)
    let pbrMaterialEntries = [new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 0u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_VERTEX | SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 1u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 2u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_SAMPLER),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 3u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 4u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 5u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE)];
    var pbrMaterialLayout = device.createBindGroupLayout(&pbrMaterialEntries);
    let pbrGroupLayouts = [&frameLayout, &pbrMaterialLayout, &environmentLayout];
    var pbrLayout = device.createPipelineLayout(&pbrGroupLayouts, IMMEDIATE_BYTES);

    // Lit: three vertex buffers (position, normal, uv), back faces culled,
    // depth tested and written
    let positionAttr = [new VertexAttribute(VERTEX_FORMAT_FLOAT32X3, 0u64, 0u32)];
    let normalAttr = [new VertexAttribute(VERTEX_FORMAT_FLOAT32X3, 0u64, 1u32)];
    let uvAttr = [new VertexAttribute(VERTEX_FORMAT_FLOAT32X2, 0u64, 2u32)];
    let litBuffers = [new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &positionAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &normalAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 8u64, attributes: &uvAttr)];
    let litDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &layout, vertexModule: &litShader, buffers: &litBuffers,
      fragmentModule: &litShader, colorFormat: colorFormat, cullMode: CULL_MODE_BACK,
      depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: true, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS);
    var litPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&litDesc);

    // Lines: positions only, depth tested (less or equal) and written
    let lineBuffers = [new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &positionAttr)];
    let linesDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &layout, vertexModule: &linesShader, buffers: &lineBuffers,
      fragmentModule: &linesShader, colorFormat: colorFormat, topology: PRIMITIVE_TOPOLOGY_LINE_LIST,
      depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: true, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS_EQUAL);
    var linesPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&linesDesc);

    // Physically based: the lit material's vertex buffers, culling and depth
    let pbrDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &pbrLayout, vertexModule: &pbrShader, buffers: &litBuffers,
      fragmentModule: &pbrShader, colorFormat: colorFormat, cullMode: CULL_MODE_BACK,
      depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: true, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS);
    var pbrPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&pbrDesc);
    // The same for a mesh with a sway stream, drawn with a flutter material:
    // the colors as a fourth buffer, read at location 3
    let swayAttr = [new VertexAttribute(VERTEX_FORMAT_FLOAT32X4, 0u64, 3u32)];
    let swayBuffers = [new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &positionAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &normalAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 8u64, attributes: &uvAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 16u64, attributes: &swayAttr)];
    let pbrSwayDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &pbrLayout, vertexModule: &pbrShader,
      vertexEntryPoint: "vertexSway", buffers: &swayBuffers, fragmentModule: &pbrShader, colorFormat: colorFormat,
      cullMode: CULL_MODE_BACK, depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: true, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS);
    var pbrSwayPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&pbrSwayDesc);
    // Their skinned variants: the same three buffers, then the joints (four
    // bytes read as integers) and the weights (four bytes read as 0 to 1)
    let jointsAttr = [new VertexAttribute(VERTEX_FORMAT_UINT8X4, 0u64, 3u32)];
    let weightsAttr = [new VertexAttribute(VERTEX_FORMAT_UNORM8X4, 0u64, 4u32)];
    let skinnedBuffers = [new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &positionAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &normalAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 8u64, attributes: &uvAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 4u64, attributes: &jointsAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 4u64, attributes: &weightsAttr)];
    let litSkinnedDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &layout, vertexModule: &litShader,
      vertexEntryPoint: "vertexSkinned", buffers: &skinnedBuffers, fragmentModule: &litShader, colorFormat: colorFormat,
      cullMode: CULL_MODE_BACK, depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: true, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS);
    var litSkinnedPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&litSkinnedDesc);
    let pbrSkinnedDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &pbrLayout, vertexModule: &pbrShader,
      vertexEntryPoint: "vertexSkinned", buffers: &skinnedBuffers, fragmentModule: &pbrShader, colorFormat: colorFormat,
      cullMode: CULL_MODE_BACK, depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: true, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS);
    var pbrSkinnedPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&pbrSkinnedDesc);
    // The see-through variants: the same, but blended with premultiplied
    // alpha (src + (1 - src alpha) x dst, the alpha likewise), the depth
    // tested and not written, so what is behind one pane still shows through
    // the next
    let litBlendDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &layout, vertexModule: &litShader, buffers: &litBuffers,
      fragmentModule: &litShader, colorFormat: colorFormat, cullMode: CULL_MODE_BACK,
      depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: false, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS,
      blendEnabled: true, colorSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, colorDstFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA,
      alphaSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, alphaDstFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA);
    var litBlendPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&litBlendDesc);
    let pbrBlendDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &pbrLayout, vertexModule: &pbrShader, buffers: &litBuffers,
      fragmentModule: &pbrShader, colorFormat: colorFormat, cullMode: CULL_MODE_BACK,
      depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: false, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS,
      blendEnabled: true, colorSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, colorDstFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA,
      alphaSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, alphaDstFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA);
    var pbrBlendPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&pbrBlendDesc);
    let litSkinnedBlendDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &layout, vertexModule: &litShader,
      vertexEntryPoint: "vertexSkinned", buffers: &skinnedBuffers, fragmentModule: &litShader, colorFormat: colorFormat,
      cullMode: CULL_MODE_BACK, depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: false, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS,
      blendEnabled: true, colorSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, colorDstFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA,
      alphaSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, alphaDstFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA);
    var litSkinnedBlendPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&litSkinnedBlendDesc);
    let pbrSkinnedBlendDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &pbrLayout, vertexModule: &pbrShader,
      vertexEntryPoint: "vertexSkinned", buffers: &skinnedBuffers, fragmentModule: &pbrShader, colorFormat: colorFormat,
      cullMode: CULL_MODE_BACK, depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: false, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS,
      blendEnabled: true, colorSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, colorDstFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA,
      alphaSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, alphaDstFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA);
    var pbrSkinnedBlendPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&pbrSkinnedBlendDesc);
    // The sky: one triangle at the far plane, where nothing nearer was
    // drawn (depth tested less or equal against the cleared 1, not written)
    let skyBuffers = [new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &positionAttr)];
    let skyDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &pbrLayout, vertexModule: &pbrShader,
      vertexEntryPoint: "backgroundVertex", buffers: &skyBuffers[..<0], fragmentModule: &pbrShader,
      fragmentEntryPoint: "backgroundFragment", colorFormat: colorFormat, depthFormat: depthFormat,
      depthWriteEnabled: false, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS_EQUAL);
    var skyPipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&skyDesc);

    var frameUniforms = device.createBuffer(FRAME_BYTES, BUFFER_USAGE_UNIFORM | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
    var instances = device.createBuffer(u64.from(FIRST_INSTANCES) * INSTANCE_BYTES,
      BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
    var bones = device.createBuffer(u64.from(FIRST_BONES) * BONE_BYTES, BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
    var boneBases = device.createBuffer(u64.from(FIRST_INSTANCES) * 4u64, BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
    var shadow = ShadowState.create(device, &materialLayout, &pbrMaterialLayout, &frameUniforms, &instances, &bones,
      &boneBases);
    let shadowView = shadow.arrayView();
    var lights = LightSet.create(device);
    let lightShadowView = lights.shadows.arrayView();
    let frameGroupEntries = [BindGroupEntry.buffer(0u32, &frameUniforms), BindGroupEntry.buffer(1u32, &instances),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(2u32, &bones), BindGroupEntry.buffer(3u32, &boneBases),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(4u32, &shadow.params), BindGroupEntry.texture(5u32, &shadowView),
      BindGroupEntry.sampler(6u32, &shadow.sampler), BindGroupEntry.buffer(7u32, &lights.paramsBuffer),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(8u32, &lights.rowBuffer), BindGroupEntry.buffer(9u32, &lights.clusterBuffer),
      BindGroupEntry.texture(10u32, &lightShadowView)];
    var frameGroup = device.createBindGroup(&frameLayout, &frameGroupEntries);
    // Trilinear, and anisotropic to 16 where the device does it (fewer
    // where it does less; none where it does none)
    let samplerDesc = new SamplerDescriptor(mipmapFilter: FILTER_MODE_LINEAR, maxAnisotropy: 16u32);
    var sampler = device.createSampler(&samplerDesc);
    let dusk = Sky.dusk(radians(4.), radians(180.));
    var environment = Environment.create(device, &environmentLayout, &dusk);

    var r = new Renderer(colorFormat, depthFormat, litShader, linesShader, frameLayout, materialLayout, layout,
      litPipeline, linesPipeline, frameUniforms, frameGroup, sampler, Pool[MeshSlot].empty(),
      Pool[TextureSlot].empty(), Pool[MaterialSlot].empty(), TextureHandle.none(), List[MeshHandle].empty(),
      0u32, 0u64, pbrShader, environmentLayout, pbrLayout, pbrPipeline, skyPipeline, environment, false, 0., 1., pbrMaterialLayout,
      instances, FIRST_INSTANCES, List[f32].empty(), List[DrawKey].empty(), List[DrawBatch].empty(), 0u32,
      Pool[PipelineSlot].empty(), litSkinnedPipeline, pbrSkinnedPipeline, bones, FIRST_BONES, boneBases,
      List[u32].empty(), 0u32, litBlendPipeline, pbrBlendPipeline, litSkinnedBlendPipeline, pbrSkinnedBlendPipeline, 0u32,
      pbrSwayPipeline, shadow, lights, List[ProbeSlot].empty(), Visibility.create(0.25), List[HiZ].empty(),
      List[DrawItem].empty(), List[SceneCapture].empty(), ReflectionSettings.medium(), List[RtScene].empty(),
      CausticVolume.none());
    var w = new Image(1, 1, 3, List[u8].empty());
    w.pixels.push(255u8);
    w.pixels.push(255u8);
    w.pixels.push(255u8);
    r.white = r.addTexture(device, &w);
    r
  }

  // Whether everything it draws with was made
  pub fn isValid(self &) bool {
    litPipeline.isValid() && linesPipeline.isValid() && frameGroup.isValid() && sampler.isValid()
      && frameUniforms.isValid() && pbrPipeline.isValid() && skyPipeline.isValid() && environment.isValid()
      && instances.isValid() && litSkinnedPipeline.isValid() && pbrSkinnedPipeline.isValid() && bones.isValid()
      && boneBases.isValid() && litBlendPipeline.isValid() && pbrBlendPipeline.isValid()
      && litSkinnedBlendPipeline.isValid() && pbrSkinnedBlendPipeline.isValid() && pbrSwayPipeline.isValid()
      && shadow.isValid() && lights.isValid()
  }

  // The frame's group made again, after a buffer in it was replaced
  fn remakeFrameGroup(self &mut, device &mut Device) {
    let shadowView = shadow.arrayView();
    let lightShadowView = lights.shadows.arrayView();
    let entries = [BindGroupEntry.buffer(0u32, &frameUniforms), BindGroupEntry.buffer(1u32, &instances),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(2u32, &bones), BindGroupEntry.buffer(3u32, &boneBases),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(4u32, &shadow.params), BindGroupEntry.texture(5u32, &shadowView),
      BindGroupEntry.sampler(6u32, &shadow.sampler), BindGroupEntry.buffer(7u32, &lights.paramsBuffer),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(8u32, &lights.rowBuffer), BindGroupEntry.buffer(9u32, &lights.clusterBuffer),
      BindGroupEntry.texture(10u32, &lightShadowView)];
    frameGroup = device.createBindGroup(&frameLayout, &entries);
    shadow.remakeCasterGroup(device, &frameUniforms, &instances, &bones, &boneBases);
  }

  // Cast the sun's shadows as 's' says (shadow.cone): off, or 1 to 4
  // cascades of the sun's shadow map of the size given, and a filter. The
  // map is made again when its size or its cascades change (the GPU is
  // waited for: set the tier at start-up or in a menu, not every frame); a
  // renderer starts with shadows off. Every lit and physically based
  // material receives them, and every opaque or cut-out mesh draw casts
  // them (a draw item marked 'dontCastShadow' does not).
  pub fn setShadows(self &mut, device &mut Device, s &ShadowSettings) {
    let wanted = clampShadowSettings(s);
    let layers = if wanted.enabled { wanted.cascades } else { 0u32 };
    let size = if wanted.enabled { wanted.mapSize } else { 1u32 };
    let wantedLayers = if layers == 0u32 { 1u32 } else { layers };
    if shadow.map.width != size || shadow.map.depthOrArrayLayers != wantedLayers {
      device.waitIdle();
      shadow.remakeMap(device, size, layers);
      self.remakeFrameGroup(device);
    }
    if wanted.slopeBias != shadow.settings.slopeBias {
      device.waitIdle();
      shadow.casters = ShadowCasters.create(device, &shadow.casterLayout, &materialLayout, &pbrMaterialLayout,
        wanted.slopeBias);
    }
    shadow.settings = wanted;
  }

  // Cast the point and spot lights' shadows as 's' says (lightshadow.cone): off,
  // or a map of 'maxViews' layers of 'tileSize' square, a spot light's view one
  // layer and a point light's six. Only a light marked 'lights.setCastsShadow'
  // casts, and the best ranked of those while layers last. The map is made
  // again when its size or layers change (the GPU is waited for: set the
  // tier at start-up or in a menu, not every frame).
  pub fn setLightShadows(self &mut, device &mut Device, s &LightShadowSettings) {
    let wanted = clampLightShadowSettings(s);
    let layers = if wanted.enabled { wanted.maxViews } else { 0u32 };
    let size = if wanted.enabled { wanted.tileSize } else { 1u32 };
    let wantedLayers = if layers == 0u32 { 1u32 } else { layers };
    if lights.shadows.map.width != size || lights.shadows.map.depthOrArrayLayers != wantedLayers {
      device.waitIdle();
      lights.shadows.remakeMap(device, size, layers);
      self.remakeFrameGroup(device);
    }
    lights.shadows.settings = wanted;
    lights.rowsDirty = true;
  }

  // The point and spot lights' shadows off again (the map is freed, the
  // one-texel stand-in kept)
  pub fn disableLightShadows(self &mut, device &mut Device) {
    let off = LightShadowSettings.off();
    self.setLightShadows(device, &off);
  }

  // Draw 'sky' behind the scene from the next render on, and light the
  // physically based material by it: its environment is made again, on the
  // GPU, at the start of that render
  pub fn setSky(self &mut, device &mut Device, sky &Sky) {
    environment.setSky(device, sky);
    drawSky = true;
  }

  // ---- Meshes ----

  // A mesh of triangles to draw: its vertex streams and indices uploaded
  // now, and kept. Normals it lacks are made smooth; uvs it lacks are 0.
  pub fn addMesh(self &mut, device &mut Device, m &Mesh) MeshHandle {
    let version = uploadTriangles(device, m);
    new MeshHandle(meshes.add(new MeshSlot(version, GpuMesh.none(), 0u32, false, 0u64, 0u32)))
  }

  // A skinned mesh to draw (skin.cone): 'm' as 'addMesh' takes it, and
  // 'skin', its vertices' joints and weights, one entry a vertex in 'm''s
  // order. Drawn by 'DrawList.addSkinned' with its bones; drawn as modelled
  // by 'add'. A skin of the wrong length leaves it an unskinned mesh.
  pub fn addSkinnedMesh(self &mut, device &mut Device, m &Mesh, skin &Skin) MeshHandle {
    let version = uploadSkinned(device, m, skin);
    new MeshHandle(meshes.add(new MeshSlot(version, GpuMesh.none(), 0u32, false, 0u64, 0u32)))
  }

  // Whether 'h' names a skinned mesh
  pub fn isSkinned(self &, h MeshHandle) bool {
    meshes.alive(h.slot) && meshes[h.slot].current().isSkinned()
  }

  // Shadows off again (the map is freed, the one-texel stand-in kept)
  pub fn disableShadows(self &mut, device &mut Device) {
    let off = ShadowSettings.off();
    self.setShadows(device, &off);
  }

  // The bounding sphere of the mesh 'h' as drawn, in its own coordinates
  // (a skinned mesh's made larger: SKINNED_BOUNDS_SCALE); a radius of 0 if
  // 'h' names none
  pub fn meshBounds(self &, h MeshHandle, center &mut Vec3, radius &mut f32) {
    if !meshes.alive(h.slot) {
      *center = new Vec3(0., 0., 0.);
      *radius = 0.;
      return;
    }
    let m = meshes[h.slot].current();
    *center = m.center;
    *radius = m.radius;
  }

  // ---- The scene (visibility.cone) ----

  // Add a thing to the scene: 'mesh' drawn with 'material' placed by 'model',
  // its color multiplied by 'tint'. Its bounds are the mesh's, now. A
  // SceneHandle names it from then on; it is drawn, culled and levelled by
  // every camera that renders. None for a mesh that is gone, skinned or lines.
  pub fn addSceneItem(self &mut, mesh MeshHandle, material MaterialHandle, model Mat4, tint Color) SceneHandle {
    if !meshes.alive(mesh.slot) { return SceneHandle.none(); }
    let m = meshes[mesh.slot].current();
    if !m.isValid() || m.topology == PRIMITIVE_TOPOLOGY_LINE_LIST || m.isSkinned() { return SceneHandle.none(); }
    let c = m.center;
    let h = m.half;
    let r = m.radius;
    vis.addItem(mesh, material, model, tint, c, h, r)
  }

  // Place a scene item anew (its proxy in the hierarchy follows)
  pub fn moveSceneItem(self &mut, h SceneHandle, model Mat4) bool { vis.move(h, model) }

  pub fn removeSceneItem(self &mut, h SceneHandle) bool { vis.remove(h) }

  pub fn clearScene(self &mut) { vis.clear(); }

  // Give a scene item the levels of 'chain' (the LodChain is copied; its
  // level 0 is the item's mesh and sets its bounds)
  pub fn setSceneLod(self &mut, h SceneHandle, chain &LodChain) bool {
    if chain.levels.len() == 0usize || !meshes.alive(chain.levels[0usize].slot) { return false; }
    let m = meshes[chain.levels[0usize].slot].current();
    let c = m.center;
    let half = m.half;
    let r = m.radius;
    if !vis.setChain(h, chain) { return false; }
    vis.setBounds(h, c, half, r)
  }

  // The bounds of an item's mesh taken again (after 'replaceMesh' gave it other bounds)
  pub fn refreshSceneItem(self &mut, h SceneHandle) bool {
    if !vis.alive(h) { return false; }
    let it = vis.items[usize.from(h.slot)];
    let mesh = it.mesh;
    if !meshes.alive(mesh.slot) { return false; }
    let m = meshes[mesh.slot].current();
    let c = m.center;
    let half = m.half;
    let r = m.radius;
    vis.setBounds(h, c, half, r)
  }

  // Visible from 'minDistance' to 'maxDistance' from the camera (0: no limit),
  // each edge fading by dither over 'margin'
  pub fn setSceneRange(self &mut, h SceneHandle, minDistance f32, maxDistance f32, margin f32) bool {
    vis.setRange(h, minDistance, maxDistance, margin)
  }

  pub fn setSceneLayers(self &mut, h SceneHandle, layers u32) bool { vis.setLayers(h, layers) }
  pub fn setSceneCastsShadow(self &mut, h SceneHandle, casts bool) bool { vis.setCastsShadow(h, casts) }
  pub fn setSceneTint(self &mut, h SceneHandle, tint Color) bool { vis.setTint(h, tint) }
  pub fn setSceneMaterial(self &mut, h SceneHandle, material MaterialHandle) bool { vis.setMaterial(h, material) }
  pub fn setSceneOccludable(self &mut, h SceneHandle, occludable bool) bool { vis.setOccludable(h, occludable) }

  // Lines to draw: 'positions', and 'indices' two to a line (a wireframe:
  // 'polyEdges' makes them of a PolyMesh's edges)
  pub fn addLines(self &mut, device &mut Device, positions &Array[Vec3], indices &Array[u32]) MeshHandle {
    let version = uploadLines(device, positions, indices);
    new MeshHandle(meshes.add(new MeshSlot(version, GpuMesh.none(), 0u32, false, 0u64, 0u32)))
  }

  // Replace what the mesh 'h' holds with 'm', under the same handle: 'm' is
  // uploaded now, and drawn from the next frame on (a frame's draws all see
  // one version); the old version's buffers are released then, and
  // destroyed once the GPU has finished the frames that drew them. Answers
  // false if 'h' names no mesh.
  pub fn replaceMesh(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MeshHandle, m &Mesh) bool {
    if !meshes.alive(h.slot) || meshes[h.slot].dynamicVertices > 0u32 { return false; }
    let version = uploadTriangles(device, m);
    self.stage(device, h, version);
    true
  }

  // The same for a skinned mesh, with its skin
  pub fn replaceSkinnedMesh(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MeshHandle, m &Mesh, skin &Skin) bool {
    if !meshes.alive(h.slot) || meshes[h.slot].dynamicVertices > 0u32 { return false; }
    let version = uploadSkinned(device, m, skin);
    self.stage(device, h, version);
    true
  }

  // The same for lines
  pub fn replaceLines(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MeshHandle, positions &Array[Vec3], indices &Array[u32]) bool {
    if !meshes.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    let version = uploadLines(device, positions, indices);
    self.stage(device, h, version);
    true
  }

  // Put 'version' into the slot of 'h' not being drawn, to be swapped in
  fn stage(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MeshHandle, version GpuMesh) {
    var slot = &mut meshes[h.slot];
    // A replacement not yet swapped in is replaced itself: it was never drawn
    if slot.active == 0u32 {
      slot.b.release(&mut device.queue);
      slot.b = version;
    } else {
      slot.a.release(&mut device.queue);
      slot.a = version;
    }
    if !slot.pending { pending.push(h); }
    slot.pending = true;
    slot.pendingFrame = device.frameNumber;
  }

  // Take the mesh 'h' away: its buffers are released (destroyed once the
  // GPU has finished with them), and the handle reaches nothing
  pub fn removeMesh(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MeshHandle) bool {
    if !meshes.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    {
      var slot = &mut meshes[h.slot];
      slot.a.release(&mut device.queue);
      slot.b.release(&mut device.queue);
    }
    meshes.remove(h.slot)
  }

  // A dynamic mesh: room for 'maxVertices' vertices and 'maxIndices'
  // indices, filled frame by frame by 'writeDynamicMesh' (a flock's birds,
  // water's waves made on the CPU). Its buffers are written in place by
  // 'queue.writeBuffer', which the GPU runs after everything submitted
  // before it, so a write never lands under a frame still drawing the last
  // contents; it is drawn only once written.
  pub fn addDynamicMesh(self &mut, device &mut Device, maxVertices u32, maxIndices u32) MeshHandle {
    var g = GpuMesh.none();
    let usage = BUFFER_USAGE_VERTEX | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_SRC;
    g.positions = device.createBuffer(u64.from(maxVertices) * 12u64, usage);
    g.normals = device.createBuffer(u64.from(maxVertices) * 12u64, usage);
    g.uvs = device.createBuffer(u64.from(maxVertices) * 8u64, usage);
    g.indices = device.createBuffer(u64.from(maxIndices) * 4u64,
      BUFFER_USAGE_INDEX | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_SRC);
    new MeshHandle(meshes.add(new MeshSlot(a: g, b: GpuMesh.none(), active: 0u32, pending: false, pendingFrame: 0u64,
      version: 0u32, dynamicVertices: maxVertices, dynamicIndices: maxIndices)))
  }

  // Fill the dynamic mesh 'h' with 'm' (normals made smooth if it has none,
  // uvs 0 if it has none), drawn by every render recorded after: write it
  // before the render that draws it, once a frame. False if 'h' is not a
  // dynamic mesh or 'm' does not fit its room.
  pub fn writeDynamicMesh(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MeshHandle, m &Mesh) bool {
    if !meshes.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    let n = m.positions.len();
    {
      let slot = meshes[h.slot];
      if slot.dynamicVertices == 0u32 || n > usize.from(slot.dynamicVertices)
          || m.indices.len() > usize.from(slot.dynamicIndices) {
        return false;
      }
    }
    var slot = &mut meshes[h.slot];
    if n == 0usize || m.indices.len() == 0usize {
      slot.a.indexCount = 0u32;
      return true;
    }
    device.queue.writeBuffer(&slot.a.positions, 0u64, bytesOf[Vec3](&m.positions), u64.from(n) * 12u64);
    if m.normals.len() == n {
      device.queue.writeBuffer(&slot.a.normals, 0u64, bytesOf[Vec3](&m.normals), u64.from(n) * 12u64);
    } else {
      var withNormals = Mesh.empty();
      withNormals.append(m);
      withNormals.computeSmoothNormals();
      device.queue.writeBuffer(&slot.a.normals, 0u64, bytesOf[Vec3](&withNormals.normals), u64.from(n) * 12u64);
    }
    if m.uvs.len() == n {
      device.queue.writeBuffer(&slot.a.uvs, 0u64, bytesOf[Vec2](&m.uvs), u64.from(n) * 8u64);
    } else {
      device.queue.clearBuffer(&slot.a.uvs, 0u64, u64.from(n) * 8u64);
    }
    device.queue.writeBuffer(&slot.a.indices, 0u64, bytesOf[u32](&m.indices), u64.from(m.indices.len()) * 4u64);
    slot.a.vertexCount = u32.from(n);
    slot.a.indexCount = u32.from(m.indices.len());
    slot.a.groups.clear();
    if m.groups.len() == 0usize {
      slot.a.groups.push(new Group(0u32, slot.a.indexCount, 0u32));
    } else {
      var i = 0usize;
      while i < m.groups.len() {
        slot.a.groups.push(*m.groups[i]);
        i = i + 1usize;
      }
    }
    boundingSphere(m.positions.view(), &mut slot.a.center, &mut slot.a.radius);
    slot.a.half = boundingHalf(m.positions.view());
    true
  }

  // Whether 'h' names a mesh
  pub fn hasMesh(self &, h MeshHandle) bool { meshes.alive(h.slot) }

  // How many times the mesh 'h' has had a replacement swapped in
  pub fn meshVersion(self &, h MeshHandle) u32 {
    if !meshes.alive(h.slot) { return 0u32; }
    meshes[h.slot].version
  }

  // What the renderer holds right now, counted from its pools: how many
  // meshes, textures, materials and custom pipelines, and the bytes of the
  // mesh buffers and of the textures (every mip level of each)
  pub fn resourceUse(self &mut) ResourceUse {
    var held = new ResourceUse(0usize, 0u64, 0usize, 0u64, 0usize, 0usize);
    {
      var it = meshes.gcTraceElements();
      var more = true;
      while more {
        match it.next() {
          case let s Some {
            held.meshes = held.meshes + 1usize;
            held.meshBytes = held.meshBytes + s.a.bufferBytes() + s.b.bufferBytes();
          }
          else { more = false; }
        }
      }
    }
    {
      var it = textures.gcTraceElements();
      var more = true;
      while more {
        match it.next() {
          case let s Some {
            held.textures = held.textures + 1usize;
            held.textureBytes = held.textureBytes + textureBytes(&s.texture);
          }
          else { more = false; }
        }
      }
    }
    held.materials = materials.len();
    held.pipelines = pipelines.len();
    held
  }

  // Swap in the replacements made in an earlier frame, releasing what they
  // replace. 'render' does this first; a program drawing no frame need not.
  pub fn update(self &mut, device &mut Device) {
    var i = 0usize;
    var kept = List[MeshHandle].empty();
    while i < pending.len() {
      let h = *pending[i];
      if meshes.alive(h.slot) {
        var slot = &mut meshes[h.slot];
        if slot.pending && device.frameNumber > slot.pendingFrame {
          if slot.active == 0u32 {
            slot.a.release(&mut device.queue);
            slot.active = 1u32;
          } else {
            slot.b.release(&mut device.queue);
            slot.active = 0u32;
          }
          slot.pending = false;
          slot.version = slot.version + 1u32;
        } elif slot.pending {
          kept.push(h);
        }
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    pending = kept;
  }

  // ---- Textures and materials ----

  // An image for materials to sample, handed to the GPU now: sRGB, four
  // channels (an RGB image's alpha opaque), its rows as the image has them,
  // bottom first, so a uv's v of 0 is its bottom row (mesh's uvs, v up)
  //
  // Every texture added here has its whole mip chain (mips.cone), made now,
  // so a surface seen small or at a slant is filtered, not aliased: colour
  // averaged in linear light.
  pub fn addTexture(self &mut, device &mut Device, img &Image) TextureHandle {
    self.addTextureAs(device, img, TEXTURE_FORMAT_RGBA8_UNORM_SRGB, MIP_COLOUR, 0.5)
  }

  // The same for a card a material cuts out below 'cutoff' of its alpha (a
  // needle tuft, a leaf, a fence; ALPHA_MASK): the colour of each level is
  // averaged weighted by the alpha, and the alpha of each is raised until the
  // same share of its texels passes 'cutoff' as the base level's do, so the
  // card does not thin to nothing as it is seen from farther off (mips.cone)
  pub fn addCutoutTexture(self &mut, device &mut Device, img &Image, cutoff f32) TextureHandle {
    self.addTextureAs(device, img, TEXTURE_FORMAT_RGBA8_UNORM_SRGB, MIP_CUTOUT, cutoff)
  }

  // The same, its bytes read as they are, not decoded from sRGB: for maps
  // that hold numbers rather than colours (glTF's metallic-roughness and
  // occlusion maps); each level averages the numbers. A normal map is
  // 'addNormalTexture'.
  pub fn addLinearTexture(self &mut, device &mut Device, img &Image) TextureHandle {
    self.addTextureAs(device, img, TEXTURE_FORMAT_RGBA8_UNORM, MIP_LINEAR, 0.5)
  }

  // A tangent-space normal map, read as it is like 'addLinearTexture', but
  // each level's vectors averaged and made unit length again, which
  // averaging the bytes would not do
  pub fn addNormalTexture(self &mut, device &mut Device, img &Image) TextureHandle {
    self.addTextureAs(device, img, TEXTURE_FORMAT_RGBA8_UNORM, MIP_NORMAL, 0.5)
  }

  fn addTextureAs(self &mut, device &mut Device, img &Image, format u32, kind u32, cutoff f32) TextureHandle {
    let w = u32.from(img.width);
    let h = u32.from(img.height);
    var rgba = List[u8].withCapacity(usize.from(w * h * 4u32));
    var p = 0usize;
    let n = usize.from(img.width * img.height);
    while p < n {
      let at = p * usize.from(img.channels);
      rgba.push(*img.pixels[at]);
      rgba.push(*img.pixels[at + 1usize]);
      rgba.push(*img.pixels[at + 2usize]);
      rgba.push(if img.channels == 4 {*img.pixels[at + 3usize]} else {255u8});
      p = p + 1usize;
    }
    let levels = if n > 0usize { mipLevelCount(w, h) } else { 1u32 };
    let desc = new TextureDescriptor(w, h, format, TEXTURE_USAGE_TEXTURE_BINDING | TEXTURE_USAGE_COPY_DST, levels);
    var texture = device.createTexture(&desc);
    if n > 0usize {
      if levels > 1u32 {
        let chain = buildMipsCut(&rgba, w, h, kind, cutoff);
        let cv = chain.view();
        device.queue.writeTextureLevels(&texture, &cv[0] as *u8);
      } else {
        let v = rgba.view();
        device.queue.writeTexture(&texture, &v[0] as *u8, w * 4u32);
      }
    }
    new TextureHandle(textures.add(new TextureSlot(texture)))
  }

  // Take the texture 'h' away, as 'removeMesh' does a mesh: its image and
  // memory are destroyed once the GPU has finished with the frames that may
  // have sampled it (no stall), and the handle reaches nothing. A material
  // made with it is not changed: remove those materials too
  // ('removeMaterial'), before they are drawn again. False for a handle that
  // reaches nothing, and for the white texture, which the renderer keeps.
  pub fn removeTexture(self &mut, device &mut Device, h TextureHandle) bool {
    if !textures.alive(h.slot) || h.slot == white.slot { return false; }
    {
      var slot = &mut textures[h.slot];
      device.queue.releaseTexture(&mut slot.texture);
    }
    textures.remove(h.slot)
  }

  // Take the material 'h' away, whatever its kind: its uniform buffer and
  // bind group are destroyed once the GPU has finished with the frames that
  // may have drawn with it (no stall), and the handle reaches nothing. A
  // draw or scene item that still names it is skipped. The textures it was
  // made with stay: remove each with 'removeTexture'.
  pub fn removeMaterial(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MaterialHandle) bool {
    if !materials.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    {
      var slot = &mut materials[h.slot];
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut slot.uniforms);
      device.queue.releaseBindGroup(&mut slot.group);
    }
    materials.remove(h.slot)
  }

  // A material to draw with: its parameters in a uniform buffer of its own,
  // bound with its texture (the white one if it has none) and the sampler
  pub fn addMaterial(self &mut, device &mut Device, material &Material) MaterialHandle {
    var uniforms = device.createBuffer(MATERIAL_BYTES, BUFFER_USAGE_UNIFORM | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
    let params = materialParams(material);
    device.queue.writeBuffer(&uniforms, 0u64, &params as *u8, MATERIAL_BYTES);
    var th = material.texture;
    if !textures.alive(th.slot) { th = white; }
    let view = textures[th.slot].texture.createView();
    let entries = [BindGroupEntry.buffer(0u32, &uniforms), BindGroupEntry.texture(1u32, &view),
      BindGroupEntry.sampler(2u32, &sampler)];
    var group = device.createBindGroup(&materialLayout, &entries);
    let pbr = PbrMaterial.standard(material.baseColor, 0., 0.5);
    new MaterialHandle(materials.add(new MaterialSlot(*material, uniforms, group, MATERIAL_BLINN_PHONG, pbr,
      PipelineHandle.none(), material.alphaMode == ALPHA_BLEND)))
  }

  // A physically based material to draw with (pbr.slang), lit by the
  // directional light and the environment made from the sky
  pub fn addPbrMaterial(self &mut, device &mut Device, material &PbrMaterial) MaterialHandle {
    if material.isExtended() { self.ensureExtended(device); }
    var uniforms = device.createBuffer(PBR_BYTES, BUFFER_USAGE_UNIFORM | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
    let params = pbrParams(material, self.mapNormalScale(material, material), self.mapOcclusionStrength(material, material));
    device.queue.writeBuffer(&uniforms, 0u64, &params as *u8, PBR_BYTES);
    let view = textures[self.orWhite(material.texture).slot].texture.createView();
    let mrView = textures[self.orWhite(material.metallicRoughnessTexture).slot].texture.createView();
    let normalView = textures[self.orWhite(material.normalTexture).slot].texture.createView();
    let occlusionView = textures[self.orWhite(material.occlusionTexture).slot].texture.createView();
    let entries = [BindGroupEntry.buffer(0u32, &uniforms), BindGroupEntry.texture(1u32, &view),
      BindGroupEntry.sampler(2u32, &sampler), BindGroupEntry.texture(3u32, &mrView),
      BindGroupEntry.texture(4u32, &normalView), BindGroupEntry.texture(5u32, &occlusionView)];
    var group = device.createBindGroup(&pbrMaterialLayout, &entries);
    let plain = Material.plain(material.baseColor);
    new MaterialHandle(materials.add(new MaterialSlot(plain, uniforms, group, MATERIAL_PBR, *material,
      PipelineHandle.none(), material.alphaMode == ALPHA_BLEND)))
  }

  // Change a physically based material's parameters (not its textures,
  // which stay those it was added with), from the next submission on
  pub fn setPbrMaterial(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MaterialHandle, material &PbrMaterial) bool {
    if !materials.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    if material.isExtended() { self.ensureExtended(device); }
    let bound = materials[h.slot].pbr;
    let params = pbrParams(material, self.mapNormalScale(&bound, material), self.mapOcclusionStrength(&bound, material));
    var slot = &mut materials[h.slot];
    if slot.kind != MATERIAL_PBR { return false; }
    device.queue.writeBuffer(&slot.uniforms, 0u64, &params as *u8, PBR_BYTES);
    slot.pbr = *material;
    slot.pbr.texture = bound.texture;
    slot.pbr.metallicRoughnessTexture = bound.metallicRoughnessTexture;
    slot.pbr.normalTexture = bound.normalTexture;
    slot.pbr.occlusionTexture = bound.occlusionTexture;
    slot.blend = material.alphaMode == ALPHA_BLEND;
    true
  }

  // Make the extended material's pipelines, capture passes and tables, if they are not made (scenecapture.cone)
  fn ensureExtended(self &mut, device &mut Device) {
    if ext.len() > 0usize { return; }
    let noRays = RtScene.none();
    ext.push(SceneCapture.create(device, colorFormat, depthFormat, &frameLayout, &pbrMaterialLayout, &environmentLayout,
      &reflections, &noRays));
  }

  // Cast rays where the card can (ray-traced glass, soap film, reflections of what is off the screen, glass-tinted
  // sunlight: raytrace.cone, rtglass.slang), or not. Chosen at run time: with 'on' and a device that has ray
  // tracing ('device.rayTracing'), the extended material is drawn by a second set of pipelines over an
  // acceleration structure the renderer builds each frame from the draw list; the material description is
  // the same, and 'setRayTracing(device, false)' returns to the raster path (glass refracting the captured
  // frame, screen-space reflections). On a card without ray tracing it does nothing and answers false: the
  // raster path draws exactly as it always did. Answers whether the next render ray traces.
  pub fn setRayTracing(self &mut, device &mut Device, on bool) bool {
    rayTracing = false;
    if !on || !device.rayTracing { return false; }
    self.ensureExtended(device);
    if ext.len() < 2usize {
      if rt.len() == 0usize { rt.push(RtScene.create(device)); }
      if !rt[0usize].isValid() { return false; }
      var traced = SceneCapture.create(device, colorFormat, depthFormat, &frameLayout, &pbrMaterialLayout,
        &environmentLayout, &reflections, rt[0usize]);
      if !traced.isValid() { return false; }
      traced.forceAll = ext[0usize].forceAll;
      traced.setCaustics(device, &causticVolume);
      ext.push(traced);
    }
    rayTracing = true;
    true
  }

  // Whether the next render casts rays (ray tracing was asked for and the card has it)
  pub fn isRayTracing(self &) bool { rayTracing && ext.len() > 1usize }

  // Screen-space reflections ray-marched as 's' says, from the next render on (a quality tier:
  // 'ReflectionSettings.high()', 'medium()', 'low()'; scenecapture.cone)
  pub fn setReflections(self &mut, s &ReflectionSettings) {
    reflections = *s;
    var k = 0usize;
    while k < ext.len() {
      var e = &mut ext[k];
      e.settings = *s;
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
  }

  // Caustics beneath a rippled surface, as 'v' says (scenecapture.cone): the sun's light focused on the
  // materials that receive it ('PbrMaterial.causticReceiver') inside the volume. 'CausticVolume.none()'
  // turns it off.
  pub fn setCaustics(self &mut, device &mut Device, v &CausticVolume) {
    self.ensureExtended(device);
    causticVolume = *v;
    var k = 0usize;
    while k < ext.len() {
      var e = &mut ext[k];
      e.setCaustics(device, v);
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
  }

  // Draw every physically based material with the extended pipelines, whether or not it needs them (a
  // test: the extended pipelines with all the lobes off must draw what the base ones do)
  pub fn forceExtended(self &mut, device &mut Device, on bool) {
    if on { self.ensureExtended(device); }
    var k = 0usize;
    while k < ext.len() {
      var e = &mut ext[k];
      e.forceAll = on;
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
  }

  // The texture 'h', or the white one if it reaches nothing
  fn orWhite(self &, h TextureHandle) TextureHandle {
    if textures.alive(h.slot) { h } else { white }
  }

  // The normal map's scale 'm' asks for, or 0 if 'bound' (the textures its
  // group holds) has no normal map; and the occlusion map's strength
  fn mapNormalScale(self &, bound &PbrMaterial, m &PbrMaterial) f32 {
    if textures.alive(bound.normalTexture.slot) { m.normalScale } else { 0. }
  }
  fn mapOcclusionStrength(self &, bound &PbrMaterial, m &PbrMaterial) f32 {
    if textures.alive(bound.occlusionTexture.slot) { m.occlusionStrength } else { 0. }
  }

  // Change a material's color, shine, glow and alpha mode (not its
  // texture), from the next submission on
  pub fn setMaterial(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MaterialHandle, material &Material) bool {
    if !materials.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    let params = materialParams(material);
    var slot = &mut materials[h.slot];
    if slot.kind != MATERIAL_BLINN_PHONG { return false; }
    device.queue.writeBuffer(&slot.uniforms, 0u64, &params as *u8, MATERIAL_BYTES);
    slot.params.baseColor = material.baseColor;
    slot.params.specular = material.specular;
    slot.params.shininess = material.shininess;
    slot.params.emissive = material.emissive;
    slot.params.alphaMode = material.alphaMode;
    slot.params.alphaCutoff = material.alphaCutoff;
    slot.params.lightLayers = material.lightLayers;
    slot.blend = material.alphaMode == ALPHA_BLEND;
    true
  }

  // ---- Custom pipelines (custom.cone) ----

  // A pipeline of the caller's own shaders, which materials made by
  // 'addCustomMaterial' are drawn with (custom.cone has the contract its
  // shaders keep). 'hasPipeline' says whether it was made.
  pub fn addPipeline(self &mut, device &mut Device, desc &CustomPipeline) PipelineHandle {
    var shader = device.createShaderModule(desc.spirv);
    let stages = SHADER_STAGE_VERTEX | SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT;
    var entries = List[BindGroupLayoutEntry].empty();
    entries.push(new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 0u32, visibility: stages));
    var t = 0usize;
    while t < desc.textures.len {
      entries.push(new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: u32.from(t) + 1u32, visibility: stages, kind: BINDING_KIND_TEXTURE,
        sampleType: desc.textures[t]));
      t = t + 1usize;
    }
    entries.push(new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: u32.from(t) + 1u32, visibility: stages, kind: BINDING_KIND_SAMPLER));
    var materialLayout = device.createBindGroupLayout(entries.view());
    var layout = if desc.environment {
      let groups = [&frameLayout, &materialLayout, &environmentLayout];
      device.createPipelineLayout(&groups, IMMEDIATE_BYTES)
    } else {
      let groups = [&frameLayout, &materialLayout];
      device.createPipelineLayout(&groups, IMMEDIATE_BYTES)
    };
    let positionAttr = [new VertexAttribute(VERTEX_FORMAT_FLOAT32X3, 0u64, 0u32)];
    let normalAttr = [new VertexAttribute(VERTEX_FORMAT_FLOAT32X3, 0u64, 1u32)];
    let uvAttr = [new VertexAttribute(VERTEX_FORMAT_FLOAT32X2, 0u64, 2u32)];
    let buffers = [new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &positionAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 12u64, attributes: &normalAttr),
      new VertexBufferLayout(arrayStride: 8u64, attributes: &uvAttr)];
    let streams = if desc.streams < 1u32 { 1usize } elif desc.streams > 3u32 { 3usize } else { usize.from(desc.streams) };
    // See-through: premultiplied alpha, the depth tested but not written
    let blend = desc.alphaMode == ALPHA_BLEND;
    let dstFactor = if blend { BLEND_FACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA } else { BLEND_FACTOR_ZERO };
    let pipelineDesc = new RenderPipelineDescriptor(layout: &layout, vertexModule: &shader,
      vertexEntryPoint: desc.vertexEntryPoint, buffers: &buffers[..<streams], fragmentModule: &shader,
      fragmentEntryPoint: desc.fragmentEntryPoint, colorFormat: colorFormat, cullMode: desc.cullMode,
      depthFormat: depthFormat, depthWriteEnabled: desc.depthWrite && !blend, depthCompare: COMPARE_FUNCTION_LESS,
      blendEnabled: blend, colorSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, colorDstFactor: dstFactor,
      alphaSrcFactor: BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, alphaDstFactor: dstFactor);
    var pipeline = device.createRenderPipeline(&pipelineDesc);
    new PipelineHandle(pipelines.add(new PipelineSlot(shader, materialLayout, layout, pipeline, u32.from(desc.textures.len),
      desc.paramBytes, desc.environment, blend)))
  }

  // Whether 'h' names a pipeline that was made
  pub fn hasPipeline(self &, h PipelineHandle) bool {
    pipelines.alive(h.slot) && pipelines[h.slot].pipeline.isValid()
  }

  // A material drawn with the custom pipeline 'pipeline': its parameters
  // 'params' (at most the pipeline's paramBytes; the rest 0) in a uniform
  // buffer of its own, and 'maps', its textures, as many as the pipeline binds (a
  // missing one is the white texture). None if 'pipeline' was not made.
  pub fn addCustomMaterial(self &mut, device &mut Device, pipeline PipelineHandle, params &Array[f32],
      maps &Array[TextureHandle]) MaterialHandle {
    if !self.hasPipeline(pipeline) { return MaterialHandle.none(); }
    let bytes = pipelines[pipeline.slot].paramBytes;
    let count = pipelines[pipeline.slot].textureCount;
    var uniforms = device.createBuffer(bytes, BUFFER_USAGE_UNIFORM | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
    self.writeParams(device, &uniforms, bytes, params);
    var views = List[TextureView].empty();
    var t = 0u32;
    while t < count {
      var th = TextureHandle.none();
      if usize.from(t) < maps.len { th = maps[usize.from(t)]; }
      views.push(textures[self.orWhite(th).slot].texture.createView());
      t = t + 1u32;
    }
    var entries = List[BindGroupEntry].empty();
    entries.push(BindGroupEntry.buffer(0u32, &uniforms));
    t = 0u32;
    while t < count {
      entries.push(BindGroupEntry.texture(t + 1u32, views[usize.from(t)]));
      t = t + 1u32;
    }
    entries.push(BindGroupEntry.sampler(count + 1u32, &sampler));
    var group = device.createBindGroup(&pipelines[pipeline.slot].materialLayout, entries.view());
    let plain = Material.plain(new Color(1., 1., 1., 1.));
    let pbr = PbrMaterial.standard(plain.baseColor, 0., 0.5);
    let blend = pipelines[pipeline.slot].blend;
    new MaterialHandle(materials.add(new MaterialSlot(plain, uniforms, group, MATERIAL_CUSTOM, pbr, pipeline, blend)))
  }

  // Change a custom material's parameters, from the next submission on
  // (its textures stay those it was made with): a water's time, say
  pub fn setCustomParams(self &mut, device &mut Device, h MaterialHandle, params &Array[f32]) bool {
    if !materials.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    let slot = materials[h.slot];
    if slot.kind != MATERIAL_CUSTOM { return false; }
    self.writeParams(device, &slot.uniforms, slot.uniforms.size, params);
    true
  }

  // Write 'params' into the first of 'bytes' bytes of 'uniforms', the rest 0
  fn writeParams(self &, device &mut Device, uniforms &Buffer, bytes u64, params &Array[f32]) {
    var data = List[f32].empty();
    let n = usize.from(bytes / 4u64);
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < n {
      data.push(if i < params.len { params[i] } else { 0. });
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    if n > 0usize {
      let v = data.view();
      device.queue.writeBuffer(uniforms, 0u64, &v[0] as *u8, bytes);
    }
  }

  // A field for a custom material to read: 'width' by 'height' numbers, one
  // f32 a texel (r32float), row by row from its first, handed to the GPU
  // now. Not every GPU filters r32float, so a shader reads it texel by
  // texel ('Load'), and its pipeline binds it as
  // TEXTURE_SAMPLE_TYPE_UNFILTERABLE_FLOAT. A heightfield, say.
  pub fn addFieldTexture(self &mut, device &mut Device, width u32, height u32, values &Array[f32]) TextureHandle {
    let desc = new TextureDescriptor(width, height, TEXTURE_FORMAT_R32_FLOAT,
      TEXTURE_USAGE_TEXTURE_BINDING | TEXTURE_USAGE_COPY_DST);
    var texture = device.createTexture(&desc);
    if values.len >= usize.from(width * height) && values.len > 0usize {
      device.queue.writeTexture(&texture, &values[0] as *u8, width * 4u32);
    }
    new TextureHandle(textures.add(new TextureSlot(texture)))
  }

  // Write all of the field 'h' again from 'values' (as many as it has),
  // ahead of the next submission: a field that changes frame by frame
  pub fn writeFieldTexture(self &mut, device &mut Device, h TextureHandle, values &Array[f32]) bool {
    if !textures.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    let slot = textures[h.slot];
    let width = slot.texture.width;
    if slot.texture.format != TEXTURE_FORMAT_R32_FLOAT || values.len < usize.from(width * slot.texture.height) {
      return false;
    }
    device.queue.writeTexture(&slot.texture, &values[0] as *u8, width * 4u32);
    true
  }

  // Write the 'width' x 'height' numbers 'values' (row by row from the first)
  // into the field 'h' at ('x', 'y'), ahead of the next submission, keeping
  // the rest of it: an atlas of patches filled as they are wanted
  // ('queue.writeTextureRegion'; the field must have been written whole once,
  // by 'addFieldTexture' with all its values or 'writeFieldTexture'). False
  // for a handle that reaches nothing, a texture that is not a field, a
  // region outside it or too few values.
  pub fn writeFieldRegion(self &mut, device &mut Device, h TextureHandle, x u32, y u32, width u32, height u32,
      values &Array[f32]) bool {
    if !textures.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    let slot = textures[h.slot];
    if slot.texture.format != TEXTURE_FORMAT_R32_FLOAT || x + width > slot.texture.width
        || y + height > slot.texture.height || values.len < usize.from(width * height) || values.len == 0usize {
      return false;
    }
    device.queue.writeTextureRegion(&slot.texture, &values[0] as *u8, width * 4u32, x, y, width, height);
    true
  }

  // ---- Drawing ----

  // Record one render pass drawing 'list' into 'target' (a texture of the
  // renderer's color format: a swapchain's, one the device made, or a
  // Post's frame), with 'depth' (the renderer's depth format, of the
  // target's size) cleared first, seen by 'camera' and lit by 'light'. The
  // target is cleared to the camera's background, and the sky drawn behind
  // the scene if one is set ('setSky'). Replacements made in an earlier
  // frame are swapped in first; the environment is made again first if the
  // sky has changed and something needs it. A draw whose mesh has been
  // removed is skipped. The frame's uniforms are one buffer, written by
  // 'queue.writeBuffer' ahead of the frame's next submission, so the passes
  // of one submission share one camera and light (a buffer a view is the
  // step when there are views).
  pub fn render(self &mut, device &mut Device, encoder &mut CommandEncoder, target &Texture, depth &Texture,
      camera &Camera, light &Light, list &DrawList) {
    let targetView = target.createView();
    let depthView = depth.createView();
    // The depth pyramid reads the depth buffer, if it can be sampled
    vis.depthSampled = (depth.usage & TEXTURE_USAGE_TEXTURE_BINDING) != 0u32;
    // The extended material captures the frame so far, if both the target and the depth can be sampled
    captureReady = vis.depthSampled && (target.usage & TEXTURE_USAGE_TEXTURE_BINDING) != 0u32 && ext.len() > 0usize;
    self.renderTo(device, encoder, targetView, depthView, camera, light, list);
    captureReady = false;
    vis.depthSampled = false;
  }

  // The same into views of the target and its depth (a view of a texture
  // the renderer itself holds a handle to, say: views.cone)
  pub fn renderTo(self &mut, device &mut Device, encoder &mut CommandEncoder, target TextureView,
      depth TextureView, camera &Camera, light &Light, list &DrawList) {
    self.update(device);
    drawCalls = 0u32;
    triangles = 0u64;
    instancesDrawn = 0u32;
    frameItemsLive = false;
    // The extended pipelines that cast rays, if ray tracing is on (setRayTracing), else the raster ones
    extActive = if rayTracing && ext.len() > 1usize && rt.len() > 0usize { 1usize } else { 0usize };
    if target.width == 0u32 || target.height == 0u32 { return; }

    // The frame's uniforms: the camera and the light
    let aspect = f32.from(target.width) / f32.from(target.height);
    let viewProjection = camera.projectionMatrix(aspect) * camera.viewMatrix();
    let inverse = viewProjection.inverse();
    let eye = camera.position();
    let towards = new Vec3(0., 0., 0.) - light.direction;
    var frame = new Array[f32, 56] <- fill 0f;
    var k = 0usize;
    while k < 16usize {
      frame[k] = viewProjection.m[k];
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    frame[16] = eye.x;
    frame[17] = eye.y;
    frame[18] = eye.z;
    frame[19] = 1.;
    frame[20] = towards.x;
    frame[21] = towards.y;
    frame[22] = towards.z;
    frame[24] = light.color.red;
    frame[25] = light.color.green;
    frame[26] = light.color.blue;
    frame[27] = 1.;
    frame[28] = light.ambient.red;
    frame[29] = light.ambient.green;
    frame[30] = light.ambient.blue;
    frame[31] = 1.;
    k = 0usize;
    while k < 16usize {
      frame[32usize + k] = inverse.m[k];
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    frame[48] = f32.from(target.width);
    frame[49] = f32.from(target.height);
    frame[50] = time;
    frame[51] = environmentStrength;
    frame[52] = exposure;
    device.queue.writeBuffer(&frameUniforms, 0u64, &frame as *u8, FRAME_BYTES);

    // The point and spot lights: assigned to this camera's clusters, and
    // written (lights.cone); the frame group is made again if the lists'
    // buffer had to grow
    if lights.prepare(device, camera, aspect, target.width, target.height) { self.remakeFrameGroup(device); }

    // The sun's cascades fitted to this camera (a function of the camera
    // alone, so the casters of each can be gathered before the batches)
    let shadowsOn = shadow.settings.enabled;
    if shadowsOn { shadow.cascades = computeCascades(camera, aspect, light.direction, &shadow.settings); }

    // The scene (visibility.cone): what this camera sees of it, added to the
    // draw list's items in a list of this render's, and, for each shadow
    // pass that is on, the casters that reach its volume, each after the
    // last. Without a scene the draw list itself is the list.
    var sceneList = DrawList.empty();
    let sceneOn = vis.active();
    var mainItems = list.items.len();
    var itemSets = List[SetRange].empty();
    if sceneOn {
      var k = 0usize;
      while k < list.items.len() {
        sceneList.items.push(*list.items[k]);
        k = k + 1usize;
      }
      k = 0usize;
      while k < list.bones.len() {
        sceneList.bones.push(*list.bones[k]);
        k = k + 1usize;
      }
      vis.collect(camera, aspect, f32.from(target.height), &mut sceneList.items);
      mainItems = sceneList.items.len();
      if vis.settings.shadowCulling {
        let localViews = lights.shadows.viewsUsed;
        let cascadeCount = if shadowsOn { shadow.cascades.count } else { 0u32 };
        var c = 0u32;
        while c < cascadeCount {
          let first = sceneList.items.len();
          self.appendCasters(&mut sceneList, list);
          let matrix = shadow.cascades.matrices[usize.from(c)];
          let volume = casterVolume(&matrix);
          vis.collectCasters(&volume, camera, f32.from(target.height), &mut sceneList.items);
          itemSets.push(new SetRange(first, sceneList.items.len()));
          c = c + 1u32;
        }
        var v = 0u32;
        while v < localViews {
          let first = sceneList.items.len();
          self.appendCasters(&mut sceneList, list);
          var matrix = Mat4.identity();
          k = 0usize;
          while k < 16usize {
            matrix.m[k] = *lights.shadows.views[usize.from(v) * 16usize + k];
            k = k + 1usize;
          }
          let volume = Frustum.fromMatrix(matrix);
          vis.collectCasters(&volume, camera, f32.from(target.height), &mut sceneList.items);
          itemSets.push(new SetRange(first, sceneList.items.len()));
          v = v + 1u32;
        }
      }
    }
    let drawList &DrawList = if sceneOn { &sceneList } else { list };

    // The batches, front to back, of the main view and then of each shadow
    // pass, and their instances and bones written
    keys.clear();
    batches.clear();
    vis.sets.clear();
    // The depth pyramid culls scene items (hiz.cone) if asked to and the depth can be sampled
    let occluding = sceneOn && vis.settings.occlusion && vis.depthSampled;
    if occluding {
      if hiz.len() == 0usize { hiz.push(HiZ.create(device, &instances, &boneBases, target.width, target.height)); }
      hiz[0usize].ensurePyramid(device, target.width, target.height);
    }
    self.gatherSet(drawList, 0usize, mainItems, eye, false, occluding);
    vis.sets.push(new SetRange(0usize, batches.len()));
    {
      var s = 0usize;
      while s < itemSets.len() {
        let firstBatch = batches.len();
        self.gatherSet(drawList, itemSets[s].first, itemSets[s].end, eye, true, false);
        vis.sets.push(new SetRange(firstBatch, batches.len()));
        s = s + 1usize;
      }
    }
    if drawSky || self.drawsPbr(drawList) { environment.bake(encoder); }
    self.writeInstances(device, drawList, occluding);
    self.writeBones(device, drawList);
    if occluding && hiz[0usize].candidateCount > 0u32 {
      var hz = &mut hiz[0usize];
      hz.upload(device, &instances, &boneBases, instanceCapacity, &viewProjection);
    }

    // The sun's shadows: their parameters written for every material to
    // read, and, if they are on, a depth pass for each cascade before the
    // scene is drawn
    {
      let place = camera.placement();
      let forward = new Vec3(-place.m[8], -place.m[9], -place.m[10]).normalize();
      let shadowFloats = shadowParamsFloats(&shadow.cascades, &shadow.settings, forward, shadowsOn);
      device.queue.writeBuffer(&shadow.params, 0u64, &shadowFloats as *u8, SHADOW_SUN_BYTES);
    }
    if shadowsOn { recordShadowPasses(self, device, encoder, drawList); }
    // And those of the point and spot lights that were given views
    recordLocalShadowPasses(self, device, encoder, drawList);

    // The background is light too: exposed like the rest
    let bg = camera.background;
    let clear = new Color(bg.red * exposure, bg.green * exposure, bg.blue * exposure, bg.alpha);
    blendedDrawn = 0u32;
    let mainEnd = vis.sets[0usize].end;
    let proj = camera.projectionMatrix(aspect);
    if ext.len() > 0usize && self.drawsPbr(drawList) {
      var e = &mut ext[extActive];
      e.bake(encoder);
    }
    // The structure rays are cast into, built from the draw list (raytrace.cone)
    if extActive == 1usize {
      var r = &mut rt[0usize];
      r.update(device, encoder, &meshes, &materials, &drawList.items, mainItems);
    }
    // With the depth pyramid, the view is drawn in two render passes with the
    // pyramid built between them (hiz.cone); otherwise in one
    let occActive = occluding && hiz[0usize].candidateCount > 0u32;
    let phases = if occActive { 2u32 } else { 1u32 };
    if occActive { hiz[0usize].recordFirst(encoder); }
    var phase = 0u32;
    while phase < phases {
    let lastPhase = phase + 1u32 == phases;
    let color = new RenderPassColorAttachment(view: target, clearValue: clear,
      loadOp: if phase == 0u32 { LOAD_OP_CLEAR } else { LOAD_OP_LOAD });
    // The extended material's captures (scenecapture.cone) end this pass to copy what it drew and begin it
    // again: 'splitMask' says which are wanted (1: before the opaque meshes that reflect the frame; 2: before
    // the glass), and the depth is stored while another capture, or the caller, will read it
    let splitMask = self.splitMask(mainEnd);
    let keepsDepth = keepDepth || !lastPhase;
    let depthStore = if keepsDepth || splitMask != 0u32 { STORE_OP_STORE } else { STORE_OP_DISCARD };
    let depthAttachment = new RenderPassDepthStencilAttachment(view: depth, depthStoreOp: depthStore,
      depthLoadOp: if phase == 0u32 { LOAD_OP_CLEAR } else { LOAD_OP_LOAD });
    var pass = encoder.beginRenderPassWithDepth(&color, &depthAttachment);
    var bound = BOUND_NONE;
    var boundMaterial = Ref[MaterialSlot].none();
    var boundPipeline = Ref[PipelineSlot].none();
    var boundProbe = 0u32;           // the probe whose group is group 2 (0: the sky's)
    var skyDrawn = !drawSky;
    var sceneLive = false;           // the capture's group (group 3) holds a capture of this render
    var reflectDone = (splitMask & 1u32) == 0u32;
    var glassDone = (splitMask & 2u32) == 0u32;
    var b = 0usize;
    while b < mainEnd {
      let batch = *batches[b];
      b = b + 1usize;
      // The first pass of two draws the opaque batches; the second draws the
      // culled ones' second set and everything after them
      if occActive {
        if phase == 0u32 && batch.layer != LAYER_OPAQUE { continue; }
        if phase == 1u32 && batch.layer == LAYER_OPAQUE && batch.occ == 0u32 { continue; }
      }
      // The opaque meshes that reflect the frame see what the others drew
      if !reflectDone && batch.layer == LAYER_OPAQUE && batch.late != 0u32 {
        pass.end();
        self.captureFrame(device, encoder, &target, &depth, &proj);
        reflectDone = true;
        sceneLive = true;
        let colorLoad = new RenderPassColorAttachment(view: target, clearValue: clear, loadOp: LOAD_OP_LOAD);
        let depthLoad = new RenderPassDepthStencilAttachment(view: depth,
          depthStoreOp: if keepsDepth || !glassDone { STORE_OP_STORE } else { STORE_OP_DISCARD }, depthLoadOp: LOAD_OP_LOAD);
        pass = encoder.beginRenderPassWithDepth(&colorLoad, &depthLoad);
        bound = BOUND_NONE;
        boundMaterial = Ref[MaterialSlot].none();
        boundPipeline = Ref[PipelineSlot].none();
      }
      // The sky, where nothing opaque was drawn, before anything
      // see-through (which writes no depth for it to be tested against)
      if batch.layer == LAYER_BLEND && !skyDrawn {
        self.recordSky(&mut pass);
        skyDrawn = true;
        bound = BOUND_NONE;
        boundMaterial = Ref[MaterialSlot].none();
      }
      // The glass sees all of that, the sky too, behind it
      if !glassDone && batch.layer == LAYER_BLEND && batch.late == 0u32 {
        pass.end();
        self.captureFrame(device, encoder, &target, &depth, &proj);
        glassDone = true;
        sceneLive = true;
        let colorLoad = new RenderPassColorAttachment(view: target, clearValue: clear, loadOp: LOAD_OP_LOAD);
        let depthLoad = new RenderPassDepthStencilAttachment(view: depth,
          depthStoreOp: if keepsDepth { STORE_OP_STORE } else { STORE_OP_DISCARD }, depthLoadOp: LOAD_OP_LOAD);
        pass = encoder.beginRenderPassWithDepth(&colorLoad, &depthLoad);
        bound = BOUND_NONE;
        boundMaterial = Ref[MaterialSlot].none();
        boundPipeline = Ref[PipelineSlot].none();
      }
      let first = *keys[usize.from(batch.first)];
      let item = drawList.items[usize.from(first.item)];
      // gatherSet kept only items whose mesh (and material) are alive
      let slot = meshes[item.mesh.slot];
      let m = slot.current();
      let lines = batch.layer == LAYER_LINES;
      let blend = batch.layer == LAYER_BLEND;
      var skinned = false;
      var sway = false;
      var tangented = false;
      if lines {
        if bound != BOUND_LINES {
          pass.setPipeline(&linesPipeline);
          pass.setBindGroup(0u32, &frameGroup);
          bound = BOUND_LINES;
        }
        // A line's model matrix and color in the immediates
        var immediates = new Array[f32, 20] <- fill 0f;
        k = 0usize;
        while k < 16usize {
          immediates[k] = item.model.m[k];
          k = k + 1usize;
        }
        immediates[16] = item.tint.red;
        immediates[17] = item.tint.green;
        immediates[18] = item.tint.blue;
        immediates[19] = item.tint.alpha;
        pass.setImmediates(0u32, &immediates as *u8, IMMEDIATE_BYTES);
      } else {
        // The material's kind chooses the pipeline
        let mslot = materials[item.material.slot];
        if mslot.kind == MATERIAL_CUSTOM {
          if bound != BOUND_CUSTOM || !(boundPipeline == mslot.pipeline.slot) {
            let ps = pipelines[mslot.pipeline.slot];
            pass.setPipeline(&ps.pipeline);
            pass.setBindGroup(0u32, &frameGroup);
            if ps.environment { pass.setBindGroup(2u32, &environment.group); }
            boundProbe = 0u32;
            bound = BOUND_CUSTOM;
            boundPipeline = mslot.pipeline.slot;
            boundMaterial = Ref[MaterialSlot].none();
          }
        } elif mslot.kind == MATERIAL_PBR {
          // A skinned mesh is drawn by the pipeline's skinned variant, a
          // see-through one by its blended variant
          skinned = m.isSkinned();
          // A material that asks for a lobe the base shader lacks, or the frame, is drawn by the extended
          // pipelines (scenecapture.cone), which have the capture as their fourth group
          let extended = ext.len() > 0usize && (mslot.pbr.isExtended() || ext[extActive].forceAll);
          // Glass found by rays replaces what is behind it, so it is drawn by a pipeline that writes depth
          let glassTraced = extended && blend && !skinned && ext[extActive].rayTraced && mslot.pbr.glass > 0.;
          // A flutter material on a mesh that carries its leaves' data
          sway = !blend && !skinned && !extended && mslot.pbr.flutter > 0. && m.sway.isValid();
          // A mesh with tangents follows them in an anisotropic highlight
          tangented = extended && !blend && !skinned && m.tangents.isValid();
          let want = if extended {
            if blend {
              if skinned { BOUND_PBRX_SKINNED_BLEND } elif glassTraced { BOUND_PBRX_GLASS } else { BOUND_PBRX_BLEND }
            } else {
              if skinned { BOUND_PBRX_SKINNED } elif tangented { BOUND_PBRX_TANGENT } else { BOUND_PBRX }
            }
          } elif blend {
            if skinned { BOUND_PBR_SKINNED_BLEND } else { BOUND_PBR_BLEND }
          } else {
            if skinned { BOUND_PBR_SKINNED } elif sway { BOUND_PBR_SWAY } else { BOUND_PBR }
          };
          if bound != want {
            if want == BOUND_PBR { pass.setPipeline(&pbrPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_PBR_SWAY { pass.setPipeline(&pbrSwayPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_PBR_SKINNED { pass.setPipeline(&pbrSkinnedPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_PBR_BLEND { pass.setPipeline(&pbrBlendPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_PBR_SKINNED_BLEND { pass.setPipeline(&pbrSkinnedBlendPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_PBRX { pass.setPipeline(&ext[extActive].opaquePipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_PBRX_SKINNED { pass.setPipeline(&ext[extActive].skinnedPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_PBRX_TANGENT { pass.setPipeline(&ext[extActive].tangentPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_PBRX_BLEND { pass.setPipeline(&ext[extActive].blendPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_PBRX_GLASS { pass.setPipeline(&ext[extActive].glassPipeline); }
            else { pass.setPipeline(&ext[extActive].skinnedBlendPipeline); }
            pass.setBindGroup(0u32, &frameGroup);
            pass.setBindGroup(2u32, &environment.group);
            if extended {
              pass.setBindGroup(3u32, if sceneLive { &ext[extActive].group } else { &ext[extActive].standInGroup });
            }
            boundProbe = 0u32;
            bound = want;
            boundMaterial = Ref[MaterialSlot].none();
          }
        } else {
          skinned = m.isSkinned();
          let want = if blend {
            if skinned { BOUND_LIT_SKINNED_BLEND } else { BOUND_LIT_BLEND }
          } else {
            if skinned { BOUND_LIT_SKINNED } else { BOUND_LIT }
          };
          if bound != want {
            if want == BOUND_LIT { pass.setPipeline(&litPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_LIT_SKINNED { pass.setPipeline(&litSkinnedPipeline); }
            elif want == BOUND_LIT_BLEND { pass.setPipeline(&litBlendPipeline); }
            else { pass.setPipeline(&litSkinnedBlendPipeline); }
            pass.setBindGroup(0u32, &frameGroup);
            bound = want;
            boundMaterial = Ref[MaterialSlot].none();
          }
        }
        if !(boundMaterial == item.material.slot) {
          pass.setBindGroup(1u32, &mslot.group);
          boundMaterial = item.material.slot;
        }
        // The environment this batch is lit by: the probe whose box holds it,
        // or the sky's (views.cone)
        if batch.probe != boundProbe && (mslot.kind == MATERIAL_PBR || (mslot.kind == MATERIAL_CUSTOM
            && pipelines[mslot.pipeline.slot].environment)) {
          if batch.probe == 0u32 {
            pass.setBindGroup(2u32, &environment.group);
          } else {
            pass.setBindGroup(2u32, &probes[usize.from(batch.probe - 1u32)].group);
          }
          boundProbe = batch.probe;
        }
      }
      pass.setVertexBuffer(0u32, &m.positions, 0u64);
      if !lines {
        pass.setVertexBuffer(1u32, &m.normals, 0u64);
        pass.setVertexBuffer(2u32, &m.uvs, 0u64);
      }
      if sway { pass.setVertexBuffer(3u32, &m.sway, 0u64); }
      if tangented { pass.setVertexBuffer(3u32, &m.tangents, 0u64); }
      if skinned {
        pass.setVertexBuffer(3u32, &m.joints, 0u64);
        pass.setVertexBuffer(4u32, &m.weights, 0u64);
      }
      pass.setIndexBuffer(&m.indices, INDEX_FORMAT_UINT32, 0u64);
      // One draw a material group of the mesh, for every copy in the batch
      var g = 0usize;
      while g < m.groups.len() {
        let group = m.groups[g];
        if lines {
          pass.drawIndexed(group.count, 1u32, group.start, 0i32, 0u32);
          triangles = triangles + u64.from(group.count / 2u32);
        } elif batch.occ != 0u32 {
          // A batch the pyramid culls: the survivors' count is the GPU's, an indirect draw (hiz.cone);
          // 'triangles' counts all its candidates, an upper bound
          let hz = hiz[0usize];
          let draw = u64.from(*hz.batchData[usize.from(batch.occ - 1u32) * 4usize + 2usize]) + u64.from(g);
          let offset = (u64.from(phase) * u64.from(hz.drawCount) + draw) * 20u64;
          pass.drawIndexedIndirect(&hz.args, offset);
          if phase == 0u32 { triangles = triangles + u64.from(group.count / 3u32) * u64.from(batch.count); }
        } else {
          pass.drawIndexed(group.count, batch.count, group.start, 0i32, batch.firstInstance);
          triangles = triangles + u64.from(group.count / 3u32) * u64.from(batch.count);
        }
        drawCalls = drawCalls + 1u32;
        g = g + 1usize;
      }
      if phase == 0u32 || batch.occ == 0u32 { instancesDrawn = instancesDrawn + batch.count; }
      if blend { blendedDrawn = blendedDrawn + batch.count; }
    }
    // The sky, where nothing was drawn, if nothing see-through came
    if !skyDrawn && lastPhase { self.recordSky(&mut pass); }
    pass.end();
    if occActive && phase == 0u32 {
      // The pyramid of what the first pass drew, and the second set of survivors
      var hz = &mut hiz[0usize];
      hz.recordSecond(device, encoder, &depth, target.width, target.height);
    }
    phase = phase + 1u32;
    }
    if occActive {
      var hz = &mut hiz[0usize];
      hz.finishFrame(&viewProjection);
      if vis.settings.occlusionStats { hz.copyStats(device, encoder); }
    }
    // The items, kept for the passes that go by the batches' keys
    frameItemsLive = sceneOn;
    if sceneOn { frameItems <=> sceneList.items; }
    frameNumber = frameNumber + 1u32;
  }

  // Which captures the batches before 'end' want (scenecapture.cone): bit 0, an opaque batch that reflects
  // the frame; bit 1, a glass batch. 0 when the render cannot capture its target.
  fn splitMask(self &, end usize) u32 {
    if !captureReady || ext.len() == 0usize { return 0u32; }
    var mask = 0u32;
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < end {
      let bt = *batches[i];
      if bt.layer == LAYER_OPAQUE && bt.late != 0u32 { mask = mask | 1u32; }
      if bt.layer == LAYER_BLEND && bt.late == 0u32 { mask = mask | 2u32; }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    mask
  }

  // Capture the target and the depth as drawn so far, for the extended material to read
  fn captureFrame(self &mut, device &mut Device, encoder &mut CommandEncoder, target &TextureView, depth &TextureView,
      proj &Mat4) {
    var e = &mut ext[extActive];
    e.capture(device, encoder, target, depth, target.width, target.height, proj.m[10], proj.m[14], frameNumber);
  }

  // Draw the sky into 'pass': one triangle at the far plane, where nothing
  // nearer was drawn
  fn recordSky(self &mut, pass &mut RenderPass) {
    pass.setPipeline(&skyPipeline);
    pass.setBindGroup(0u32, &frameGroup);
    pass.setBindGroup(2u32, &environment.group);
    pass.draw(3u32, 1u32, 0u32, 0u32);
    drawCalls = drawCalls + 1u32;
  }

  // The reflection probe whose box holds the point 'p': 1 + its index (the
  // smallest box if several hold it), or 0 if none does (views.cone)
  fn probeFor(self &, p Vec3) u32 {
    var found = 0u32;
    var volume = 0.f;
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < probes.len() {
      let s = probes[i];
      if s.ready && p.x >= s.boxMin.x && p.x <= s.boxMax.x && p.y >= s.boxMin.y && p.y <= s.boxMax.y
          && p.z >= s.boxMin.z && p.z <= s.boxMax.z {
        if found == 0u32 || s.volume < volume {
          found = u32.from(i) + 1u32;
          volume = s.volume;
        }
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    found
  }

  // Whether 'list' draws a mesh with a physically based material
  fn drawsPbr(self &, list &DrawList) bool {
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < list.items.len() {
      let item = list.items[i];
      if materials.alive(item.material.slot) {
        let mslot = materials[item.material.slot];
        if mslot.kind == MATERIAL_PBR { return true; }
        if mslot.kind == MATERIAL_CUSTOM && pipelines.alive(mslot.pipeline.slot) {
          if pipelines[mslot.pipeline.slot].environment { return true; }
        }
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    false
  }

  // Gather 'list's items into 'batches', in the order they are drawn: an
  // item of a mesh and material that are alive gets a key, in its layer
  // (opaque meshes, lines, see-through); the keys are sorted by layer, then
  // the opaque ones and lines by (material, mesh, distance), so each run of
  // one material and one mesh is a batch (a line is a batch of its own), and
  // the see-through ones by distance alone, farthest from the camera at
  // 'eye' first, each copy by the centre of its bounding sphere where the
  // copy puts it (a large pane is mis-sorted by its origin), so a batch of
  // them is a run of copies of one mesh and material that are next to each
  // other in that order. The batches are then sorted by layer, the opaque
  // ones and lines nearest first (by the nearest of their models' origins),
  // so nearer surfaces fill the depth buffer first; the see-through ones keep
  // their order, back to front.
  //
  // Only the items 'itemFirst' to 'itemEnd' are gathered, their keys and
  // batches added after those already there (each set sorted by itself): the
  // main view's, then a shadow pass's, which 'shadowOnly' limits to what
  // casts a shadow (no lines, nothing see-through or custom).
  fn gatherSet(self &mut, list &DrawList, itemFirst usize, itemEnd usize, eye Vec3, shadowOnly bool, occlusion bool) {
    var setKeys = List[DrawKey].withCapacity(itemEnd - itemFirst);
    var i = itemFirst;
    while i < itemEnd {
      let item = list.items[i];
      let cast = if item.castsShadow { 1u32 } else { 0u32 };
      if meshes.alive(item.mesh.slot) {
        let m = meshes[item.mesh.slot].current();
        if m.isValid() {
          if shadowOnly {
            if m.topology != PRIMITIVE_TOPOLOGY_LINE_LIST && materials.alive(item.material.slot)
                && casterKindOf(self, item, m) != CASTER_NONE {
              let d = item.model.translation().distanceSquared(eye);
              setKeys.push(new DrawKey(LAYER_OPAQUE, item.material.slot.slot(), item.mesh.slot.slot(), u32.from(i), 1u32, d, 0u32));
            }
          } elif m.topology == PRIMITIVE_TOPOLOGY_LINE_LIST {
            let d = item.model.translation().distanceSquared(eye);
            setKeys.push(new DrawKey(LAYER_LINES, u32.from(i), item.mesh.slot.slot(), u32.from(i), 0u32, d, 0u32));
          } elif materials.alive(item.material.slot) {
            let probe = self.probeFor(item.model.translation());
            let mslot = materials[item.material.slot];
            let extended = mslot.kind == MATERIAL_PBR;
            if mslot.blend {
              let d = (item.model * m.center).distanceSquared(eye);
              // Glass is drawn before the rest of the see-through meshes (scenecapture.cone): 'late' 0
              let late = if extended && mslot.pbr.glass > 0. { 0u32 } else { 1u32 };
              setKeys.push(new DrawKey(LAYER_BLEND, item.material.slot.slot(), item.mesh.slot.slot(), u32.from(i), 0u32, d, probe,
                0u32, late));
            } else {
              let d = item.model.translation().distanceSquared(eye);
              // The depth pyramid may cull an unskinned lit or physically based copy the scene marked so
              let occ = if occlusion && item.occludable && !m.isSkinned() && mslot.kind != MATERIAL_CUSTOM
                { 1u32 } else { 0u32 };
              // A mesh that reflects the frame is drawn after the others (scenecapture.cone): 'late' 1
              let late = if extended && mslot.pbr.reflections > 0. { 1u32 } else { 0u32 };
              setKeys.push(new DrawKey(LAYER_OPAQUE, item.material.slot.slot(), item.mesh.slot.slot(), u32.from(i), cast, d, probe,
                occ, late));
            }
          }
        }
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    // A big set (thousands of scene items in a handful of batches) is grouped
    // by (material, mesh, ...) with a hash, a counting sort, in a pass; the
    // comparison sort below would cost n log n compares of 40-byte keys. Only
    // opaque keys group this way: they keep their order in the list within
    // a batch (not nearest first, which only helps early depth rejection),
    // each batch's distance the nearest of its keys'. Everything else, and a
    // small set, sorts as ever.
    var placed = List[DrawKey].empty();
    var groupCount = List[u32].empty();
    var groupNear = List[f32].empty();
    var groupRep = List[DrawKey].empty();
    var groupOffset = List[u32].empty();
    if setKeys.len() > bucketMin {
      var rest = List[DrawKey].empty();
      var big = List[DrawKey].withCapacity(setKeys.len());
      var s = 0usize;
      while s < setKeys.len() {
        let key = *setKeys[s];
        if key.layer == LAYER_OPAQUE && key.material < 1048576u32 && key.mesh < 1048576u32 && key.probe < 4096u32
            && key.late == 0u32 {
          big.push(key);
        } else {
          rest.push(key);
        }
        s = s + 1usize;
      }
      setKeys = rest;
      var ids = Dict[u64, u32].empty();
      var groupOf = List[u32].withCapacity(big.len());
      s = 0usize;
      while s < big.len() {
        let key = *big[s];
        let packed = (u64.from(key.material) << 44u64) | (u64.from(key.mesh) << 24u64) | (u64.from(key.probe) << 12u64)
          | (u64.from(key.cast & 1u32) << 1u64) | u64.from(key.occ & 1u32);
        var id = 0u32;
        if ids.containsKey(&packed) {
          id = *ids[&packed];
          groupCount.set(usize.from(id), *groupCount[usize.from(id)] + 1u32);
          if key.distance < *groupNear[usize.from(id)] { groupNear.set(usize.from(id), key.distance); }
        } else {
          id = u32.from(groupCount.len());
          ids.insert(packed, id);
          groupCount.push(1u32);
          groupNear.push(key.distance);
          groupRep.push(key);
        }
        groupOf.push(id);
        s = s + 1usize;
      }
      var running = 0u32;
      s = 0usize;
      while s < groupCount.len() {
        groupOffset.push(running);
        running = running + *groupCount[s];
        s = s + 1usize;
      }
      if big.len() > 0usize {
        placed = List[DrawKey].withCapacity(big.len());
        placed.resize(big.len(), *big[0usize]);
        var cursor = List[u32].withCapacity(groupOffset.len());
        s = 0usize;
        while s < groupOffset.len() {
          cursor.push(*groupOffset[s]);
          s = s + 1usize;
        }
        s = 0usize;
        while s < big.len() {
          let g = usize.from(*groupOf[s]);
          placed.set(usize.from(*cursor[g]), *big[s]);
          cursor.set(g, *cursor[g] + 1u32);
          s = s + 1usize;
        }
      }
    }
    setKeys.sortBy(&byBatch);
    // Runs of one material and mesh
    let keyBase = keys.len();
    var setBatches = List[DrawBatch].empty();
    var k = 0usize;
    while k < setKeys.len() {
      let first = *setKeys[k];
      var end = k + 1usize;
      while end < setKeys.len() && setKeys[end].layer == first.layer && setKeys[end].material == first.material
          && setKeys[end].mesh == first.mesh && setKeys[end].cast == first.cast && setKeys[end].probe == first.probe
          && setKeys[end].occ == first.occ && setKeys[end].late == first.late {
        end = end + 1usize;
      }
      // The keys of a run are sorted nearest first (or, see-through,
      // farthest first)
      var runBatch = new DrawBatch(u32.from(keyBase + k), u32.from(end - k), 0u32, first.distance, first.layer,
        u32.from(keyBase + k), first.layer == LAYER_OPAQUE && first.cast == 0u32, first.probe, first.occ);
      runBatch.late = first.late;
      setBatches.push(runBatch);
      k = end;
    }
    // The grouped keys' batches, their keys after the sorted ones
    k = 0usize;
    while k < groupCount.len() {
      let rep = *groupRep[k];
      let at = u32.from(keyBase + setKeys.len()) + *groupOffset[k];
      setBatches.push(new DrawBatch(at, *groupCount[k], 0u32, *groupNear[k], LAYER_OPAQUE, at, rep.cast == 0u32,
        rep.probe, rep.occ));
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    setBatches.sortBy(&byDistance);
    k = 0usize;
    while k < setKeys.len() {
      keys.push(*setKeys[k]);
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    k = 0usize;
    while k < placed.len() {
      keys.push(*placed[k]);
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    k = 0usize;
    while k < setBatches.len() {
      batches.push(*setBatches[k]);
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
  }

  // The items of 'list' that cast a shadow, copied onto the end of 'frame'
  // (a shadow pass's set holds the draw list's own items whole, beside the
  // scene's it gathers)
  fn appendCasters(self &, frame &mut DrawList, list &DrawList) {
    var k = 0usize;
    while k < list.items.len() {
      let it = list.items[k];
      if it.castsShadow { frame.items.push(*it); }
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
  }

  // Write every batch's copies (model matrix and tint) into the instance
  // buffer side by side, in the order the batches are drawn, and give each
  // batch its first instance; the buffer is made larger first if it must be
  //
  // With the depth pyramid on ('occluding'), the copies of a batch it may cull
  // do not go in here: they are the candidates of its culling pass (hiz.cone),
  // and the batch has two places in the buffer after all the others, one for
  // each draw, for the GPU to fill with the survivors.
  fn writeInstances(self &mut, device &mut Device, list &DrawList, occluding bool) {
    instanceData.clear();
    boneBaseData.clear();
    var count = 0u32;
    var b = 0usize;
    var occTotal = 0u32;
    while b < batches.len() {
      var batch = *batches[b];
      if batch.occ != 0u32 {
        occTotal = occTotal + batch.count;
        b = b + 1usize;
        continue;
      }
      batch.firstInstance = count;
      batches.set(b, batch);
      var j = 0u32;
      while j < batch.count {
        let item = list.items[usize.from(keys[usize.from(batch.first + j)].item)];
        var e = 0usize;
        while e < 16usize {
          instanceData.push(item.model.m[e]);
          e = e + 1usize;
        }
        instanceData.push(item.tint.red);
        instanceData.push(item.tint.green);
        instanceData.push(item.tint.blue);
        instanceData.push(item.tint.alpha);
        // An unskinned copy's word carries its fade, if it has one (fade.slang)
        boneBaseData.push(if item.fade != 0. && item.bones == NO_BONES { fadeCode(item.fade) } else { item.bones });
        j = j + 1u32;
      }
      count = count + batch.count;
      b = b + 1usize;
    }
    let plain = count;
    if occTotal > 0u32 && occluding {
      // The culled batches: two places each after the rest, a candidate for each copy
      var place0 = plain;
      var place1 = plain + occTotal;
      var hz = &mut hiz[0usize];
      hz.beginFrame();
      b = 0usize;
      while b < batches.len() {
        var batch = *batches[b];
        if batch.occ != 0u32 {
          let firstItem = list.items[usize.from(keys[usize.from(batch.first)].item)];
          let gm = meshes[firstItem.mesh.slot].current();
          let index = hz.addBatch(place0, place1, gm);
          batch.occ = index + 1u32;
          batch.firstInstance = place0;
          batch.dest2 = place1;
          batches.set(b, batch);
          var j = 0u32;
          while j < batch.count {
            let item = list.items[usize.from(keys[usize.from(batch.first + j)].item)];
            let mm = meshes[item.mesh.slot].current();
            let box = Aabb3.fromCenter(mm.center, mm.half).transformed(item.model);
            let word = if item.fade != 0. && item.bones == NO_BONES { fadeCode(item.fade) } else { item.bones };
            hz.addCandidate(index, box.center(), box.halfExtents(), &item.model, item.tint, word);
            j = j + 1u32;
          }
          place0 = place0 + batch.count;
          place1 = place1 + batch.count;
        }
        b = b + 1usize;
      }
      count = plain + 2u32 * occTotal;
    }
    if count == 0u32 { return; }
    if count > instanceCapacity {
      var capacity = instanceCapacity;
      while capacity < count { capacity = capacity * 2u32; }
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut instances);
      instances = device.createBuffer(u64.from(capacity) * INSTANCE_BYTES, BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut boneBases);
      boneBases = device.createBuffer(u64.from(capacity) * 4u64, BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
      instanceCapacity = capacity;
      self.remakeFrameGroup(device);
    }
    if plain > 0u32 {
      let v = instanceData.view();
      device.queue.writeBuffer(&instances, 0u64, &v[0] as *u8, u64.from(plain) * INSTANCE_BYTES);
      let bv = boneBaseData.view();
      device.queue.writeBuffer(&boneBases, 0u64, &bv[0] as *u8, u64.from(plain) * 4u64);
    }
  }

  // Write the draw list's bones (every skinned copy's skinning matrices,
  // side by side) into the bone buffer, made larger first if it must be
  fn writeBones(self &mut, device &mut Device, list &DrawList) {
    let count = u32.from(list.bones.len() / BONE_FLOATS);
    bonesDrawn = count;
    if count == 0u32 { return; }
    if count > boneCapacity {
      var capacity = boneCapacity;
      while capacity < count { capacity = capacity * 2u32; }
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut bones);
      bones = device.createBuffer(u64.from(capacity) * BONE_BYTES, BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
      boneCapacity = capacity;
      self.remakeFrameGroup(device);
    }
    let v = list.bones.view();
    device.queue.writeBuffer(&bones, 0u64, &v[0] as *u8, u64.from(count) * BONE_BYTES);
  }
}

// An item of the draw list, as batching sorts it
pub struct DrawKey {
  layer u32;                   // LAYER_OPAQUE, LAYER_LINES (each alone) or LAYER_BLEND
  material u32;                // its material's slot (a line: its own index, so it batches with nothing)
  mesh u32;                    // its mesh's slot
  item u32;                    // its index in the draw list
  cast u32;                    // 1 if it casts the sun's shadow, 0 if not: a batch holds one or the other
  // Its distance from the eye, squared: its model's origin's, or, if it is
  // see-through, its bounding sphere's centre's
  distance f32;
  probe u32;                   // the reflection probe that lights it, 1 + its index; 0: the sky's
  occ u32 = 0u32;              // 1 if the depth pyramid may cull it (hiz.cone): a batch holds all or none
  // 1 if it is drawn after the rest of its layer: an opaque mesh that reflects the frame, a see-through mesh that is
  // not glass (glass, 0, is drawn first, so what blends over it blends over its refraction); scenecapture.cone
  late u32 = 0u32;
}

// One instanced draw: 'count' keys from 'first', drawn as the instances
// from 'firstInstance' in the instance buffer
pub struct DrawBatch {
  first u32;
  count u32;
  firstInstance u32;
  distance f32;                // its nearest copy's distance from the eye, squared (see-through: its farthest's)
  layer u32;
  order u32;                   // its first key's place among the sorted keys
  noShadow bool;               // its copies cast no shadow
  probe u32;                   // its copies' reflection probe (DrawKey)
  occ u32 = 0u32;              // 1 + its place among the batches the depth pyramid culls (hiz.cone); 0: not culled
  dest2 u32 = 0u32;            // the second draw's first instance, for such a batch (firstInstance is the first draw's)
  late u32 = 0u32;             // its keys' (DrawKey)
}

fn byBatch(a &DrawKey, b &DrawKey) i32 {
  if a.layer != b.layer { return if a.layer < b.layer { -1i32 } else { 1i32 }; }
  if a.late != b.late { return if a.late < b.late { -1i32 } else { 1i32 }; }
  if a.layer == LAYER_BLEND {
    // Back to front, copy by copy; ties by the item's place in the list
    if a.distance > b.distance { return -1i32; }
    if a.distance < b.distance { return 1i32; }
    return if a.item < b.item { -1i32 } elif a.item > b.item { 1i32 } else { 0i32 };
  }
  if a.material != b.material { return if a.material < b.material { -1i32 } else { 1i32 }; }
  if a.mesh != b.mesh { return if a.mesh < b.mesh { -1i32 } else { 1i32 }; }
  if a.cast != b.cast { return if a.cast < b.cast { -1i32 } else { 1i32 }; }
  if a.probe != b.probe { return if a.probe < b.probe { -1i32 } else { 1i32 }; }
  if a.occ != b.occ { return if a.occ < b.occ { -1i32 } else { 1i32 }; }
  if a.distance < b.distance { return -1i32; }
  if a.distance > b.distance { return 1i32; }
  0i32
}

fn byDistance(a &DrawBatch, b &DrawBatch) i32 {
  if a.layer != b.layer { return if a.layer < b.layer { -1i32 } else { 1i32 }; }
  if a.late != b.late { return if a.late < b.late { -1i32 } else { 1i32 }; }
  if a.layer == LAYER_BLEND {
    // Kept in the keys' order, back to front
    return if a.order < b.order { -1i32 } elif a.order > b.order { 1i32 } else { 0i32 };
  }
  if a.distance < b.distance { return -1i32; }
  if a.distance > b.distance { return 1i32; }
  0i32
}

// A material's parameters as lit.slang's MaterialParams has them
fn materialParams(material &Material) Array[f32, 16] {
  [material.baseColor.red, material.baseColor.green, material.baseColor.blue, material.baseColor.alpha,
    material.specular.red, material.specular.green, material.specular.blue, material.shininess,
    material.emissive.red, material.emissive.green, material.emissive.blue, 0.,
    f32.from(material.alphaMode), material.alphaCutoff, f32.from(material.lightLayers & 16777215u32), 0.]
}

// What a draw list holds: a mesh, the material it is drawn with (not used
// by lines), where it is ('model', its coordinates into the world's), and a
// tint its color is multiplied by (the color of lines); and, for a skinned
// copy, its first bone in the list's 'bones' (NO_BONES for none)
pub struct DrawItem {
  pub mesh MeshHandle;
  pub material MaterialHandle;
  pub model Mat4;
  pub tint Color;
  pub bones u32 = NO_BONES;
  pub layers u32 = 1u32;       // the layers it is on: a view draws the items its layer mask meets (views.cone)
  // Whether it casts the sun's shadow (shadow.cone), if it is the kind that
  // does: an opaque or cut-out lit or physically based mesh
  pub castsShadow bool = true;
  // How much of it is drawn, by dither (fade.slang): 0 whole; above 0 fading
  // out by that share; below 0 fading in to that share. Visibility sets it
  // for a cross-fade between levels and a visibility range's edge; it rides
  // in the instance's per-instance word, so it is for an unskinned copy.
  pub fade f32 = 0.;
  // Whether the depth pyramid may cull it (hiz.cone)
  pub occludable bool = false;
}

// What a render pass draws: its items, and the skinned ones' bones, each
// bone a skinning matrix as the bone buffer holds it (skin.cone's
// 'boneRows', BONE_FLOATS floats), each item's run side by side
pub struct DrawList {
  pub items List[DrawItem];
  pub bones List[f32];

  pub fn empty() DrawList { new DrawList(List[DrawItem].empty(), List[f32].empty()) }

  pub fn clear(self &mut) {
    items.clear();
    bones.clear();
  }
  pub fn len(self &) usize { items.len() }

  // How many bones it holds
  pub fn boneCount(self &) usize { bones.len() / BONE_FLOATS }

  // Draw the skinned mesh 'mesh' ('Renderer.addSkinnedMesh') with
  // 'material', placed by 'model', posed by 'pose': its skinning matrices,
  // one a bone of its skin's skeleton, in the model's coordinates (skin.cone)
  pub fn addSkinned(self &mut, mesh MeshHandle, material MaterialHandle, model Mat4, pose &Array[Mat4]) {
    self.addSkinnedTinted(mesh, material, model, new Color(1., 1., 1., 1.), pose);
  }

  // The same, its color multiplied by 'tint'
  pub fn addSkinnedTinted(self &mut, mesh MeshHandle, material MaterialHandle, model Mat4, tint Color, pose &Array[Mat4]) {
    let first = u32.from(bones.len() / BONE_FLOATS);
    var b = 0usize;
    while b < pose.len {
      let rows = boneRows(pose[b]);
      var e = 0usize;
      while e < BONE_FLOATS {
        bones.push(rows[e]);
        e = e + 1usize;
      }
      b = b + 1usize;
    }
    items.push(new DrawItem(mesh, material, model, tint, first));
  }

  // Put the items from index 'from' on (those just added) on the layers
  // 'mask' (a bit a layer; items start on layer bit 0)
  pub fn setLayers(self &mut, from usize, mask u32) {
    var i = from;
    while i < items.len() {
      var it = *items[i];
      it.layers = mask;
      items.set(i, it);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
  }

  // The last item added casts no shadow (a ground that only receives them,
  // a skybox, a mesh far from the sun's use)
  pub fn dontCastShadow(self &mut) {
    if items.len() == 0usize { return; }
    var last = *items[items.len() - 1usize];
    last.castsShadow = false;
    items.set(items.len() - 1usize, last);
  }

  // Draw 'mesh' with 'material', placed by 'model'
  pub fn add(self &mut, mesh MeshHandle, material MaterialHandle, model Mat4) {
    items.push(new DrawItem(mesh, material, model, new Color(1., 1., 1., 1.)));
  }

  // The same, its color multiplied by 'tint'
  pub fn addTinted(self &mut, mesh MeshHandle, material MaterialHandle, model Mat4, tint Color) {
    items.push(new DrawItem(mesh, material, model, tint));
  }

  // Draw the lines 'mesh' in 'color', placed by 'model'
  pub fn addLines(self &mut, mesh MeshHandle, model Mat4, color Color) {
    items.push(new DrawItem(mesh, MaterialHandle.none(), model, color));
  }
}
